"You could have told me earlier!","example_es":"Tu aurais pu me le dire plus tôt !","difficulty":1,"tags":["modals","regret"]},{"id":"efr-guilty","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u06","text":"guilty","translation_es":"coupable","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/ˈɡɪlti/","romanization":null,"emoji":"😞","example_en":"I feel guilty about what I said.","example_es":"Je me sens coupable de ce que j’ai dit.","difficulty":1,"tags":["emotions","adjectives"]},{"id":"efr-fall-out","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u06","text":"fall out","translation_es":"se brouiller / se fâcher (avec quelqu’un)","accepted_translations":["se quereller","se fâcher avec quelqu’un","se disputer","se brouiller"],"ipa":"/ˈfɔl ˈaʊt/","romanization":null,"emoji":"💢","example_en":"I fell out with my best friend last week.","example_es":"La semaine dernière, je me suis fâchée avec ma meilleure amie.","difficulty":1,"tags":["relationships","phrasal-verbs"]},{"id":"efr-make-up","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u06","text":"make up","translation_es":"se réconcilier / faire la paix","accepted_translations":["se réconcilier","faire la paix","se rabibocher"],"ipa":"/ˈmeɪk ˈʌp/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🤝","example_en":"They argued, but they made up the next day.","example_es":"Ils se sont disputés, mais ils se sont réconciliés le lendemain.","difficulty":1,"tags":["relationships","phrasal-verbs"]},{"id":"efr-overreact","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u06","text":"overreact","translation_es":"exagérer / réagir de façon excessive","accepted_translations":["exagérer","réagir de façon excessive","en faire trop","dramatiser"],"ipa":"/ˌoʊvəriˈækt/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"I'm sorry I overreacted. It wasn't a big problem.","example_es":"Désolé d’avoir exagéré. Ce n’était pas grave.","difficulty":1,"tags":["relationships","verbs"]},{"id":"efr-take-it-personally","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u06","text":"take it personally","translation_es":"le prendre pe