 / biaisé","accepted_translations":["partial","biaisé","tendancieux"],"ipa":"/ˈbaɪəst/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"The article is biased. It only shows one side.","example_es":"L’article est partial. Il ne montre qu’un seul côté.","difficulty":1,"tags":["media","adjectives"]},{"id":"efr-misleading","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u08","text":"misleading","translation_es":"trompeur","accepted_translations":["fallacieux"],"ipa":"/mɪsˈlidɪŋ/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"The numbers in the post are misleading.","example_es":"Les chiffres de la publication sont trompeurs.","difficulty":1,"tags":["media","adjectives"]},{"id":"efr-fact-check","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u08","text":"fact-check","translation_es":"vérifier (les faits)","accepted_translations":["vérifier","vérifier les faits"],"ipa":"/ˈfækt ˌtʃɛk/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🔍","example_en":"Always fact-check a story before you share it.","example_es":"Vérifie toujours une info avant de la partager.","difficulty":1,"tags":["media","verbs"]},{"id":"efr-audience","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u08","text":"audience","translation_es":"public / audience","accepted_translations":["public","audience","spectateurs"],"ipa":"/ˈɔdiəns/","romanization":null,"emoji":"👥","example_en":"The program has a large audience.","example_es":"L’émission a un large public.","difficulty":1,"tags":["media"]},{"id":"efr-would-have","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u09","text":"would have","translation_es":"aurais / serais (+ participe)","accepted_translations":["aurais","serais","aurait","serait"],"ipa":"/ˈwʊd əv/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"If I had studied, I would have passed the exam.","example_es":"Si j’avais étudié, j’aurais réussi l’examen.","difficulty":1,"tags":["conditionals"]},{"id":"efr-if-only","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u09","text":"if only","translation_es":"si seulement","accepted_translations":["pourvu que"],"ipa":"