ll week. As a result, the match was canceled.","example_es":"Il a plu toute la semaine. Par conséquent, le match a été annulé.","difficulty":1,"tags":["connectors","argument"]},{"id":"efr-what-matters-is","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u10","text":"what matters is","translation_es":"ce qui compte, c’est","accepted_translations":["l’important, c’est","ce qui importe, c’est"],"ipa":"/wʌt ˈmætərz ɪz/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"What matters is that you tried.","example_es":"Ce qui compte, c’est que tu aies essayé.","difficulty":1,"tags":["cleft-sentences"]},{"id":"efr-the-reason-why","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u10","text":"the reason why","translation_es":"la raison pour laquelle","accepted_translations":["le motif pour lequel","si… c’est parce que"],"ipa":"/ðə ˈrizən waɪ/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"The reason why I called is that I need your help.","example_es":"La raison pour laquelle j’ai appelé, c’est que j’ai besoin de ton aide.","difficulty":1,"tags":["cleft-sentences"]},{"id":"efr-in-other-words","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u10","text":"in other words","translation_es":"en d’autres termes / autrement dit","accepted_translations":["en d’autres termes","autrement dit","c’est-à-dire","bref"],"ipa":"/ɪn ˈʌðər ˈwɜrdz/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"He was late again. In other words, he does not care.","example_es":"Il est encore arrivé en retard. Autrement dit, ça lui est égal.","difficulty":1,"tags":["connectors","argument"]},{"id":"efr-admittedly","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u10","text":"admittedly","translation_es":"certes / il faut reconnaître que","accepted_translations":["certes","il faut reconnaître que","il est vrai que","je reconnais que"],"ipa":"/ədˈmɪtɪdli/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"Admittedly, it is expensive.","example_es":"Certes, c’est cher.","difficulty":1,"tags":["connectors","argument"]},{"id":"efr-nevertheless","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u10","text":"nevertheless","translation_es":"néanmoins / malgré tout","accepted_translations":["malgré tout","toutefois","néanmoins","pourtant","cependant","quand même"],"ipa":"/ˌnɛvərðəˈlɛs/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"It was difficult. Nevertheless, we finished on time.","example_es":"C’était difficile. Néanmoins, nous avons fini à temps.","difficulty":1,"tags":["connectors","argument"]},{"id":"efr-on-the-contrary","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u10","text":"on the contrary","translation_es":"au contraire","accepted_translations":["bien au contraire"],"ipa":"/ɑn ðə ˈkɑnˌtrɛri/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🔄","example_en":"I'm not tired. On the contrary, I feel great.","example_es":"Je ne suis pas fatigué. Au contraire, je me sens super bien.","difficulty":1,"tags":["connectors","argument"]},{"id":"efr-point-of-view","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u10","text":"point of view","translation_es":"point de vue","accepted_translations":["un point de vue","avis"],"ipa":"/ˈpɔɪnt əv ˈvju/","romanization":null,"emoji":"👁️","example_en":"I understand your point of view, but I disagree.","example_es":"Je comprends ton point de vue, mais je ne suis pas d’accord.","difficulty":1,"tags":["argument"]},{"id":"efr-valid","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u10","text":"valid","translation_es":"valable / valide","accepted_translations":["valable","valide","pertinent"],"ipa":"/ˈvælɪd/","romanization":null,"emoji":"✔️","example_en":"That's a valid point.","example_es":"C’est un argument valable.","difficulty":1,"tags":["argument","adjectives"]},{"id":"efr-convincing","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u10","text":"convincing","translation_es":"convaincant","accepted_translations":["convaincante","persuasif"],"ipa":"/kənˈvɪnsɪŋ/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"Her argument was very convincing.","example_es":"Son argument était très convaincant.","difficulty":1,"tags":["argument","adjectives"]},{"id":"efr-assumption","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u10","text":"assumption","translation_es":"supposition / hypothèse","accepted_translations":["supposition","présupposé","une supposition","une hypothèse"],"ipa":"/əˈsʌmpʃən/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"That's just an assumption. Where is the evidence?","example_es":"Ce n’est qu’une supposition. Où sont les preuves ?","difficulty":1,"tags":["argument"]},{"id":"efr-take-into-account","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u10","text":"take into account","translation_es":"tenir compte de / prendre en compte","accepted_translations":["prendre en compte","tenir compte de","prendre en considération"],"ipa":"/ˈteɪk ˈɪntu əˈkaʊnt/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🧮","example_en":"We need to take the costs into account.","example_es":"Nous devons tenir compte des coûts.","difficulty":1,"tags":["argument","collocations"]},{"id":"efr-outweigh","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u10","text":"outweigh","translation_es":"l’emporter sur / peser plus lourd que","accepted_translations":["l’emporter sur","peser plus lourd que","compenser largement"],"ipa":"/aʊtˈweɪ/","romanization":null,"emoji":"⚖️","example_en":"The benefits outweigh the costs.","example_es":"Les avantages l’emportent sur les coûts.","difficulty":1,"tags":["argument","verbs"]},{"id":"efr-to-sum-up","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u10","text":"to sum up","translation_es":"en résumé / pour résumer","accepted_translations":["en résumé","pour résumer","bref","en somme"],"ipa":"/tə ˈsʌm ˈʌp/","romanization":null,"emoji":"📝","example_en":"To sum up, I think the plan is a good idea.","example_es":"En résumé, je pense que le plan est une bonne idée.","difficulty":1,"tags":["connectors","argument"]},{"id":"efr-all-things-considered","language_code":"en","unit_id":"efr-b2-u10","text":"all things considered","translation_es":"tout bien considéré / tout compte fait","accepted_translations":["après tout","tout compte fait","tout bien considéré","au bou