me souviens pas de son nom.","options":["meeting","to meet","meet","met"]},"answer":"meeting","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Remember + -ing : le souvenir de quelque chose qui s’est déjà passé.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-remember-doing"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l03-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Please remember ___ the door when you leave.","translation":"S’il te plaît, pense à fermer la porte quand tu pars.","options":["to close","closing","close","closed"]},"answer":"to close","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Remember + to : quelque chose que tu dois faire.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-remember-doing"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l03-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"We were tired, so we stopped ___ a coffee.","translation":"On était fatigués, alors on s’est arrêtés pour prendre un café.","options":["to have","having","have","had"]},"answer":"to have","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Stop + to : s’arrêter pour faire autre chose. Stop + -ing : arrêter de le faire.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-remember-doing"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l03-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l03","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I regret ___ those things to my brother.","translation":"Je regrette d’avoir dit ces choses à mon frère.","options":["saying","to say","say","said"]},"answer":"saying","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Regret + -ing : tu regrettes quelque chose que tu as fait.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-regret"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l03-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u1-apology","document":"email","setting":"Un e-mail qui essaie de dissiper un malentendu.","from":"Nina","to":"Mark","title":"About my email","lines":["Hi Mark,","I want to apologize for my email yesterday. I realize it sounded rude, and I regret writing it in such a hurry.","I did not mean to criticize your work. Actually, the report is very good. I only wanted to show you one mistake in the numbers before the meeting.","Next time I will stop to think before I click \"send\". If you have a minute today, I would be happy to talk about it.","Best wishes,","Nina"]},"question":"Que regrette Nina ?","options":["D’avoir écrit l’e-mail trop vite","D’avoir critiqué le rapport","De ne pas être allée à la réunion","D’avoir appelé Mark"]},"answer":"D’avoir écrit l’e-mail trop vite","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Nina écrit : « I regret writing it in such a hurry ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l03-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u1-apology","document":"email","setting":"Un e-mail qui essaie de dissiper un malentendu.","from":"Nina","to":"Mark","title":"About my email","lines":["Hi Mark,","I want to apologize for my email yesterday. I realize it sounded rude, and I regret writing it in such a hurry.","I did not mean to criticize your work. Actually, the report is very good. I only wanted to show you one mistake in the numbers before the meeting.","Next time I will stop to think before I click \"send\". If you have a minute today, I would be happy to talk about it.","Best wishes,","Nina"]},"question":"Que fera Nina la prochaine fois ?","options":["S’arrêter pour réfléchir avant de cliquer sur « envoyer »","Arrêter d’envoyer des e-mails","Demander à Mark de relire ses e-mails","Écrire plus vite"]},"answer":"S’arrêter pour réfléchir avant de cliquer sur « envoyer »","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Nina écrit : « Next time I will stop to think before I click \"send\" » (stop + to = s’arrêter pour).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l03-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l03","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"I regret saying those things to my brother.","options":["I regret saying those things to my brother.","I regret saying those things to my mother.","I don't regret saying those things to my brother.","I regret not saying those things to my brother."]},"answer":"I regret saying those things to my brother.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-regret"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l03-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l03","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Remets les mots dans l’ordre","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Remember","to","call","your","grandmother","tonight"],"translation":"Pense à appeler ta grand-mère ce soir."},"answer":"Remember to call your grandmother tonight.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["efr-remember-doing"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l03-e09","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l03","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Réponds en anglais","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Are you still smoking? (tu as arrêté de fumer il y a deux ans)","translation":"Tu fumes ?"},"answer":"No, I stopped smoking two years ago.","accepted_answers":["I stopped smoking two years ago.","No, I stopped two years ago.","No. I stopped smoking two years ago."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-remember-doing"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l03-e10","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Je me souviens de l’avoir rencontrée, mais j’ai oublié de lui demander son nom."},"answer":"I remember meeting her, but I forgot to ask her name.","accepted_answers":["I remember meeting her but I forgot to ask her name.","I remember meeting her, but I forgot to ask her what her name was."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-remember-doing"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l04-e01","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Associe chaque mot à sa signification","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"straightforward","right":"direct / franc"},{"left":"blunt","right":"brusque / trop direct"},{"left":"tactful","right":"plein de tact / diplomate"},{"left":"bring up","right":"aborder (un sujet) / mentionner"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-straightforward","efr-blunt","efr-tactful","efr-bring-up"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l04-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"She pointed ___ a mistake in my report.","translation":"Elle a signalé une erreur dans mon rapport.","options":["out","up","on","off"]},"answer":"out","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-point-out"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l04-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Sorry to be ___, but your plan won’t work.","translation":"Désolé d’être aussi direct, mais ton plan ne va pas marcher.","options":["blunt","tactful","polite","friendly"]},"answer":"blunt","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Blunt : si direct que ça peut mal passer. On l’emploie pour s’excuser avant une critique.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-blunt"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l04-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l04","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"People ___ speak faster when they are nervous.","translation":"Les gens ont tendance à parler plus vite quand ils sont nerveux.","options":["tend to","seem","mean to","used"]},"answer":"tend to","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-tend-to"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l04-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u1-feedback-post","document":"post","setting":"Un article de blog sur la façon de donner un avis difficile.","title":"How to say difficult things","lines":["Most of us tend to avoid difficult conversations. We are afraid of hurting people, so we say nothing, or we drop a hint and hope the other person understands.","The problem is that hints are easy to miss. Your colleague may not realize there is a problem at all.","Being straightforward does not mean being blunt. Start with something positive, then point out the problem clearly and calmly, and finally look for a solution together.","Remember: people can accept honest feedback when it is tactful. What they find hard to accept is sarcasm."]},"question":"D’après le texte, quel est le problème des allusions ?","options":["On peut facilement passer à côté","Elles sont impolies","Elles prennent beaucoup de temps","Elles blessent toujours"]},"answer":"On peut facilement passer à côté","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Le texte dit : « The problem is that hints are easy to miss ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l04-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u1-feedback-post","document":"post","setting":"Un article de blog sur la façon de donner un avis difficile.","title":"How to say difficult things","lines":["Most of us tend to avoid difficult conversations. We are afraid of hurting people, so we say nothing, or we drop a hint and hope the other person understands.","The problem is that hints are easy to miss. Your colleague may not realize there is a problem at all.","Being straightforward does not mean being blunt. Start with something positive, then point out the problem clearly and calmly, and finally look for a solution together.","Remember: people can accept honest feedback when it is tactful. What they find hard to accept is sarcasm."]},"question":"Quelle différence le texte fait-il entre straightforward et blunt ?","options":["On peut être clair sans être brusque","C’est la même chose","Être brusque marche mieux","Il faut éviter d’être clair"]},"answer":"On peut être clair sans être brusque","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Le texte dit : « Being straightforward does not mean being blunt ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l04-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l04","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u1-feedback-post","document":"post","setting":"Un article de blog sur la façon de donner un avis difficile.","title":"How to say difficult things","lines":["Most of us tend to avoid difficult conversations. We are afraid of hurting people, so we say nothing, or we drop a hint and hope the other person understands.","The problem is that hints are easy to miss. Your colleague may not realize there is a problem at all.","Being straightforward does not mean being blunt. Start with something positive, then point out the problem clearly and calmly, and finally look for a solution together.","Remember: people can accept honest feedback when it is tactful. What they find hard to accept is sarcasm."]},"question":"D’après le texte, qu’est-ce que les gens acceptent le moins bien ?","options":["Le sarcasme","Un avis sincère","Un commentaire positif","Une solution trouvée ensemble"]},"answer":"Le sarcasme","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Le texte dit : « people can accept honest feedback when it is tactful. What they find hard to accept is sarcasm ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l04-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l04","position":8,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Don't bring up politics at dinner.","options":["Don't bring up politics at dinner.","Don't bring up politics at work.","Do bring up politics at dinner.","Don't talk about politics at dinner."]},"answer":"Don't bring up politics at dinner.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-bring-up"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l04-e09","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l04","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Réponds en anglais","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Should I tell him about the problem? (oui, mais avec tact)","translation":"Je lui parle du problème ?"},"answer":"Yes, but be tactful.","accepted_answers":["Yes, but try to be tactful.","Yes, but you should be tactful.","Yes. But be tactful."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-tactful"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u01-l04-e10","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u01-l04","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Elle a signalé une erreur dans mon rapport."},"answer":"S