 this flexibility is important to me.","I would be happy to accept a slightly lower salary, provided that I can keep those two days at home. Otherwise, I am afraid I would have to turn the offer down.","I hope we can reach an agreement. I am free to talk at any time this week.","Kind regards,","Laura Kim"]},"question":"Quelle condition Laura pose-t-elle pour accepter l’offre ?","options":["Continuer à télétravailler deux jours par semaine","Un salaire plus élevé","Commencer le mois prochain","Avoir sa propre équipe"]},"answer":"Continuer à télétravailler deux jours par semaine","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Laura écrit : « I would be happy to accept a slightly lower salary, provided that I can keep those two days at home ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u02-l03-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u02-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u2-offer","document":"email","setting":"Une candidate répond à une offre d’emploi.","from":"Laura Kim","to":"Mr. Patel","title":"Job offer","lines":["Dear Mr. Patel,","Thank you very much for the job offer. I am very excited about joining the team.","Before I accept, I would like to discuss one point. In my current job I work from home two days a week, and this flexibility is important to me.","I would be happy to accept a slightly lower salary, provided that I can keep those two days at home. Otherwise, I am afraid I would have to turn the offer down.","I hope we can reach an agreement. I am free to talk at any time this week.","Kind regards,","Laura Kim"]},"question":"Que se passe-t-il si l’entreprise n’accepte pas sa condition ?","options":["Laura va refuser l’offre","Laura va accepter quand même","Laura va demander plus de temps","Laura va parler à son chef actuel"]},"answer":"Laura va refuser l’offre","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Laura écrit : « Otherwise, I am afraid I would have to turn the offer down ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u02-l03-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u02-l03","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Send me the terms in writing, in case anything changes.","options":["Send me the terms in writing, in case anything changes.","Send me the terms in writing, as long as nothing changes.","Send me the terms by email, in case anything changes.","Send them the terms in writing, in case anything changes."]},"answer":"Send me the terms in writing, in case anything changes.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-in-case"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u02-l03-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u02-l03","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Remets les mots dans l’ordre","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["I","will","help","you","as","long","as","you","help","me"],"translation":"Je vais t’aider tant que tu m’aides."},"answer":"I will help you as long as you help me.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["efr-as-long-as"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u02-l03-e09","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u02-l03","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Réponds en anglais","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Why are you taking a jacket? (au cas où il ferait froid)","translation":"Pourquoi tu prends une veste ?"},"answer":"In case it gets cold.","accepted_answers":["In case it's cold.","I am taking it in case it gets cold.","I'm taking a jacket in case it gets cold."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-in-case"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u02-l03-e10","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u02-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Dépêche-toi. Sinon, on va rater le train."},"answer":"Hurry up. Otherwise, we will miss the train.","accepted_answers":["Hurry up. Otherwise, we'll miss the train.","Hurry up. Otherwise we will miss the train.","Hurry up, otherwise we'll miss the train."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-otherwise"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u02-l04-e01","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u02-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Associe chaque mot à sa signification","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"leader","right":"leader / dirigeant"},{"left":"delegate","right":"déléguer"},{"left":"workload","right":"charge de travail"},{"left":"persuade","right":"convaincre / persuader"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-leader","efr-delegate","efr-workload","efr-persuade"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u02-l04-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u02-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"She took ___ a new project last week.","translation":"Elle a pris en charge un nouveau projet la semaine dernière.","options":["on","up","off","down"]},"answer":"on","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-take-on"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u02-l04-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u02-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I persuaded my boss ___ me a day off.","translation":"J’ai convaincu mon chef de me donner un jour de congé.","options":["to give","giving","give","gave"]},"answer":"to give","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Persuade someone to + verbe (convaincre quelqu’un de + infinitif).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-persuade"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u02-l04-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u02-l04","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u2-team","setting":"Une cheffe d’équipe parle avec un employé débordé.","speakers":[{"name":"Grace","voice":"a"},{"name":"Omar","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Grace","text":"Omar, you look exhausted. Is your workload too heavy at the moment?"},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Honestly, yes. I took on the new client last month, and I'm still doing my old projects."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"You should have told me. A good leader needs to know these things."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"I didn't want to turn down the client. I thought it was a good opportunity."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"It is, but you can't do everything. Let's delegate the reports to Ben."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Are you sure? He is quite new."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"That's fine. I'll help him at the beginning, in case he has questions."}]},"question":"Pourquoi Omar a-t-il autant de travail ?","options":["Il a pris en charge un nouveau client et continue ses anciens projets","Un collègue a démissionné","Il apprend un nouveau métier","Sa cheffe lui a donné les rapports de Ben"]},"answer":"Il a pris en charge un nouveau client et continue ses anciens projets","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Omar dit : « I took on the new client last month, and I’m still doing my old projects ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u02-l04-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u02-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u2-team","setting":"Une cheffe d’équipe parle avec un employé débordé.","speakers":[{"name":"Grace","voice":"a"},{"name":"Omar","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Grace","text":"Omar, you look exhausted. Is your workload too heavy at the moment?"},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Honestly, yes. I took on the new client last month, and I'm still doing my old projects."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"You should have told me. A good leader needs to know these things."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"I didn't want to turn down the client. I thought it was a good opportunity."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"It is, but you can't do everything. Let's delegate the reports to Ben."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Are you sure? He is quite new."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"That's fine. I'll help him at the beginning, in case he has questions."}]},"question":"Quelle solution Grace propose-t-elle ?","options":["Déléguer les rapports à Ben et l’aider au début","Refuser le nouveau client","Embaucher quelqu’un d’autre","Qu’Omar travaille le week-end"]},"answer":"Déléguer les rapports à Ben et l’aider au début","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Grace dit : « Let’s delegate the reports to Ben… I’ll help him at the beginning ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u02-l04-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u02-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u2-leader","document":"post","setting":"Un article de magazine sur le leadership.","title":"Leaders, not bosses","lines":["What makes a good leader? Many people imagine someone who gives orders and never changes their mind. Research shows the opposite.","The best leaders are flexible. They listen first, and they are willing to compromise when a better idea appears.","They also know how to delegate. Instead of doing everything themselves, they give people responsibility and trust them to do the job.","Finally, they persuade rather than order. When a team understands the reason for a decision, it works harder to make it succeed."]},"question":"D’après l’article, pourquoi vaut-il mieux convaincre que donner des ordres ?","options":["Parce qu’une équipe qui comprend la raison travaille davantage pour que la décision réussisse","Parce que les ordres sont illégaux","Parce que comme ça, le leader travaille moins","Parce que l’équipe a toujours raison"]},"answer":"Parce qu’une équipe qui comprend la raison travaille davantage pour que la décision réussisse","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’article dit : « When a team understands the reason for a decision, it works harder to make it succeed ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u02-l04-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u02-l04","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"A good leader listens to the team.","options":["A good leader listens to the team.","A good leader talks to the team.","A good leader listens to the client.","The good leaders listen to the team."]},"answer":"A good leader listens to the team.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-leader"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u02-l04-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u02-l04","position":8,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u2-leader","document":"post","setting":"Un article de magazine sur le leadership.","title":"Leaders, not bosses","lines":["What makes a good leader? Many people imagine someone who gives orders and never changes their mind. Research shows the opposite.","The best leaders are flexible. They listen first, and they are willing to compromise when a better idea appears.","They also know how to delegate. Instead of doing everything themselves, they give people responsibility and trust them to do the job.","Finally, they persuade rather than order. When a team understands the reason for a decision, it works harder to make it succeed."]},"question":"D’après l’article, comment sont les meilleurs leaders ?","options":["Flexibles : ils é