plète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"In some countries it is a ___ to take off your shoes at home.","translation":"Dans certains pays, c’est la coutume d’enlever ses chaussures à la maison.","options":["custom","trend","society","habit"]},"answer":"custom","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Custom : coutume d’une société. Habit : habitude d’une personne.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-custom"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u03-l01-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u03-l01","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Un podcast interviewe une sociologue sur les générations.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"D’après la sociologue, que dit chaque génération de la suivante ?","options":["Qu’elle ne respecte pas les coutumes d’autrefois","Qu’elle travaille plus","Qu’elle vit mieux","Qu’elle est plus heureuse"]},"answer":"Qu’elle ne respecte pas les coutumes d’autrefois","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’animateur demande si les jeunes ne respectent pas les coutumes, et elle répond : « Every generation has said that about the next one ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u03-l01-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u03-l01","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Un podcast interviewe une sociologue sur les générations.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"D’après la sociologue, qu’est-ce qui a changé et qu’est-ce qui n’a pas changé ?","options":["Les coutumes ont changé, mais pas les valeurs","Les valeurs ont changé, mais pas les coutumes","Rien n’a changé","Tout a changé"]},"answer":"Les coutumes ont changé, mais pas les valeurs","accepte