 be","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Be expected + to + verbe.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-be-expected-to"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u03-l03-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u03-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"It is a ___ idea, but it is not true.","translation":"C’est une idée très répandue, mais elle n’est pas vraie.","options":["widespread","average","local","lonely"]},"answer":"widespread","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-widespread"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u03-l03-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u03-l03","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Un podcast interviewe une sociologue sur les générations.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"Pourquoi la sociologue parle-t-elle des Grecs de l’Antiquité ?","options":["Pour montrer que se plaindre des jeunes ne date pas d’hier","Pour parler de l’histoire de la Grèce","Pour dire que les Grecs étaient meilleurs","Pour expliquer une coutume grecque"]},"answer":"Pour montrer que se plaindre des jeunes ne date pas d’hier","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Elle dit : « It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u03-l03-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u03-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Un podcast interviewe une sociologue sur les générations.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"Que pense la sociologue de l’idée que le fossé entre les générations se creuse ?","options":["Que beaucoup de gens le croient, mais que ses recherches ne le confirment pas","Qu’elle est vraie","Que c’est une idée nouvelle","Que personne n’y croit"]},"answer":"Que beaucoup de gens le croient, mais que ses recherches ne le confirment pas","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Elle dit : « Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u03-l03-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u03-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u3-market","document":"notice","setting":"Un avis de la mairie sur le vieux marché.","title":"Our market is changing","lines":["The old market is being renovated and will be closed until the end of May.","The roof has already been repaired, and new lights are being installed this month.","The market has been used by local families for more than a hundred years. It is believed to be the oldest building in the neighborhood.","When the work is finished, the market will be used for concerts and festivals. The first festival is expected to take place in June.","Questions can be sent to the community office."]},"question":"Que pense-t-on du marché ?","options":["Que c’est le plus vieux bâtiment du quartier","Qu’il va fermer définitivement","Que c’est le plus grand de la ville","Qu’il a été construit par une famille"]},"answer":"Que c’est le plus vieux bâtiment du quartier","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’avis dit : « It is believed to be the oldest building in the neighborhood ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u03-l03-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u03-l03","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"It is said that the house is two hundred years old.","options":["