epted_answers":["Housing is really expensive in big cities.","In big cities, housing is very expensive.","Housing is very expensive in large cities."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-housing"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u03-rev2-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u03-rev2","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Réponds en anglais","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"When will the homes be ready? (ils devraient être prêts l’année prochaine)","translation":"Quand les logements seront-ils prêts ?"},"answer":"They are expected to be ready next year.","accepted_answers":["They're expected to be ready next year.","They are expected to be finished next year.","Next year, they are expected to be ready."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-be-expected-to"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u03-rev2-e09","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u03-rev2","position":9,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"widespread","options":["widespread","population","majority","housing"]},"answer":"widespread","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-widespread"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u03-rev2-e10","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u03-rev2","position":10,"type":"complete_word","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Écris le mot en entier","payload":{"type":"complete_word","masked":"i_ b_i_g b_i_t","hint":"est en construction / on construit"},"answer":"is being built","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":20,"words":["efr-being-built"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u03-l05-e01","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u03-l05","position":1,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Que veut dire « diversity » ?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"diversity","options":["diversité","société","tendance","population"]},"answer":"diversité","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["efr-diversity"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u03-l05-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u03-l05","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"More homes should ___ built for young people.","translation":"On devrait construire plus de logements pour les jeunes.","options":["be","being","been","to be"]},"answer":"be","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Passif avec un modal : should / can / will + be + participe.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-housing"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u03-l05-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u03-l05","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Many languages can be ___ in the market.","translation":"Au marché, on peut entendre beaucoup de langues.","options":["heard","hear","hearing","hears"]},"answer":"heard","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-diversity"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u03-l05-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u03-l05","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Un podcast interviewe une sociologue sur les générations.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"D’après la sociologue, comment les jeunes montrent-ils aujourd’hui qu’ils tiennent à leur famille ?","options":["Autrement, par exemple avec un appel vidéo au lieu d’un déjeuner","Ils ne le montrent plus","En vivant chez leurs parents","En allant à l’église"]},"answer":"Autrement, par exemple avec un appel vidéo au lieu d’un déjeuner","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Elle dit : « They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u03-l05-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u03-l05","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u3-market","document":"notice","setting":"Un avis de la mairie sur le vieux marché.","title":"Our market is changing","lines":["The old market is being renovated and will be closed until the end of May.","The roof has already been repaired, and new lights are being installed this month.","The market has been used by local families for more than a hundred years. It is believed to be the oldest building in the neighborhood.","When the work is finished, the market will be used for concerts and festivals. The first festival is expected to take place in June.","Questions can be sent to the community office."]},"question":"À quoi servira le marché à la fin des travaux ?","options":["À des concerts et des festivals","À des logements","À des bureaux","À une école"]},"answer":"À des concer