y villages, most of which have no clean water. The data are very clear."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What is the next step?"},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"We want to make it in large numbers. The invention is useless if the people who need it can't get it."}]},"question":"Qu’est-ce que le filtre de Mei Lin a de spécial ?","options":["Il est bon marché et nettoie l’eau seulement avec la lumière du soleil","C’est le plus grand du monde","Il marche à l’électricité","C’est l’animateur qui l’a inventé"]},"answer":"Il est bon marché et nettoie l’eau seulement avec la lumière du soleil","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Mei dit : « Our filter, which costs less than five dollars, uses only sunlight to clean dirty water ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u04-l02-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u04-l02","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u4-interview","setting":"Une interview à la radio d’une scientifique qui a inventé un filtre à eau.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Mei","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"My guest today is Dr. Mei Lin, whose team has come up with a new way to clean water. Welcome."},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"Thank you. Our filter, which costs less than five dollars, uses only sunlight to clean dirty water."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"That sounds like a real breakthrough. How did you get the idea?"},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"By accident, actually. One of our experiments failed, which was very frustrating at the time. But the results showed something we didn't expect."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is there evidence that it works outside the lab?"},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"Yes. We have tested it in forty villages, most of which have no clean water. The data are very clear."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What is the next step?"},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"We want to make it in large numbers. The invention is useless if the people who need it can't get it."}]},"question":"Que veut dire Mei par « The invention is useless if the people who need it can’t get it » ?","options":["Que l’invention ne sert que si elle arrive à ceux qui en ont besoin","Que l’invention ne marche pas","Que c’est très cher","Que personne n’en a besoin"]},"answer":"Que l’invention ne sert que si elle arrive à ceux qui en ont besoin","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"C’est pour ça que la prochaine étape est de le fabriquer en grande quantité : « We want to make it in large numbers ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u04-l02-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u04-l02","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u4-museum","document":"notice","setting":"Des panneaux dans une salle d’un musée des sciences.","title":"Science Museum","lines":["Room 3: Ideas that changed the world","The telephone, which was invented in 1876, allowed people to talk across long distances for the first time.","Marie Curie, whose discoveries changed medicine, was the first person to win two Nobel Prizes.","The World Wide Web was created by Tim Berners-Lee, a scientist for whom sharing information was more important than money. He never asked for payment for his invention.","Which of these innovations do you use every day?"]},"question":"Qu’est-ce qui est mis en avant à propos de Tim Berners-Lee ?","options":["Que partager l’information comptait plus pour lui que l’argent","Qu’il a inventé le téléphone","Qu’il a gagné deux prix Nobel","Qu’il a fait payer cher son invention"]},"answer":"Que partager l’information comptait plus pour lui que l’argent","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Le panneau dit : « a scientist for whom sharing information was more important than money. He never asked for payment ».","difficulty":1,"recommende