oducts we buy and even helps doctors read X-rays.","Most of us rely on it every day without thinking about it. That is exactly the problem.","To work well, these systems need huge amounts of data, much of which comes from our phones. Every search, every photo and every location can be stored, which raises serious questions about privacy.","This does not mean we should reject innovation. But we should know who collects our data, how it is used and for how long it is kept.","Technology is a tool. Whether it helps or harms us depends on the rules we decide to give it."]},"question":"Selon l’auteur, quel est « exactement le problème » ?","options":["Que nous dépendons de l’IA tous les jours sans y penser","Que l’IA coûte très cher","Que les médecins ne l’utilisent pas","Que l’IA choisit mal les chansons"]},"answer":"Que nous dépendons de l’IA tous les jours sans y penser","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’article dit : « Most of us rely on it every day without thinking about it. That is exactly the problem ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u04-l04-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u04-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u4-ai","document":"post","setting":"Un article d’opinion sur l’intelligence artificielle.","title":"Who is watching the machines?","lines":["Artificial intelligence is everywhere: it chooses the songs we listen to, suggests the products we buy and even helps doctors read X-rays.","Most of us rely on it every day without thinking about it. That is exactly the problem.","To work well, these systems need huge amounts of data, much of which comes from our phones. Every search, every photo and every location can be stored, which raises serious questions about privacy.","This does not mean we should reject innovation. But we should know who collects our data, how it is used and for how long it is kept.","Technology is a tool. Whether it helps or harms us depends on the rules we decide to give it."]},"question":"Pourquoi l’IA pose-t-elle des questions sur la vie privée ?","options":["Parce qu’elle a besoin de beaucoup de données, dont une grande partie vient de nos téléphones","Parce qu’elle est très lente","Parce qu’elle ne marche pas sans internet","Parce que les banques l’utilisent"]},"answer":"Parce qu’elle a besoin de beaucoup de données, dont une grande partie vient de nos téléphones","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’article dit : « these systems need huge amounts of data, much of which comes from our phones… which raises serious questions about privacy ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u04-l04-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u04-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u4-ai","document":"post","setting":"Un article d’opinion sur l’intelligence artificielle.","title":"Who is watching the machines?","lines":["Artificial intelligence is everywhere: it chooses the songs we listen to, suggests the products we buy and even helps doctors read X-rays.","Most of us rely on it every day without thinking about it. That is exactly the problem.","To work well, these systems need huge amounts of data, much of which comes from our phones. Every search, every photo and every location can be stored, which raises serious questions about privacy.","This does not mean we should reject innovation. But we should know who collects our data, how it is used and for how long it is kept.","Technology is a tool. Whether it helps or harms us depends on the rules we decide to give it."]},"question":"Quelle est la position de l’auteur sur l’innovation ?","options":["Il ne faut pas la rejeter, mais il faut savoir comment nos données sont utilisées","Il faut l’interdire","Elle ne présente aucun risque","Seuls les mé