on":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"We are having our kitchen ___ next month.","translation":"Le mois prochain, nous allons faire peindre notre cuisine.","options":["painted","paint","painting","to paint"]},"answer":"painted","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-have-something-done"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u05-l03-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u05-l03","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u5-repair","setting":"Un client dans une boutique de réparation de téléphones.","speakers":[{"name":"Customer","voice":"a"},{"name":"Assistant","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Customer","text":"Hi. I dropped my phone yesterday and I'd like to have the screen replaced."},{"speaker":"Assistant","text":"Let me see. Yes, we can do that. It's ninety dollars, and it'll be ready tomorrow."},{"speaker":"Customer","text":"Ninety? That's twice as much as I paid last time!"},{"speaker":"Assistant","text":"Last time you had a cheaper screen put in. This one is original. The cheaper ones are nowhere near as good."},{"speaker":"Customer","text":"Hmm. Is it worth it? The phone is three years old."},{"speaker":"Assistant","text":"Honestly, the older the phone, the less sense it makes. A new one costs about four hundred."},{"speaker":"Customer","text":"I can't afford a new one right now. Go ahead and replace the screen, please."}]},"question":"Que veut le client ?","options":["Faire changer l’écran de son téléphone","Acheter un nouveau téléphone","Se faire rembourser","Réparer l’écran lui-même"]},"answer":"Faire changer l’écran de son téléphone","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Le client dit : « I’d like to have the screen replaced ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u05-l03-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u05-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u5-flatmates","setting":"Deux colocataires parlent d’argent.","speakers":[{"name":"Jake","voice":"a"},{"name":"Rita","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Jake","text":"I'm thinking of taking out a loan to buy a car."},{"speaker":"Rita","text":"Are you sure? You still have debt on your credit card."},{"speaker":"Jake","text":"I know, but the bank is offering a low interest rate at the moment."},{"speaker":"Rita","text":"Low now, but it could rise. And can you really afford the monthly payments?"},{"speaker":"Jake","text":"If I cut back on eating out, I think so."},{"speaker":"Rita","text":"Why not buy a second-hand car instead? You'd need a much smaller loan, or no loan at all."},{"speaker":"Jake","text":"That's actually a good idea. I'll have a mechanic check a few cars this weekend."}]},"question":"Que va faire Jake ce week-end ?","options":["Faire vérifier quelques voitures par un mécanicien","Vérifier lui-même les voitures","Demander le prêt","Vendre sa voiture"]},"answer":"Faire vérifier quelques voitures par un mécanicien","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Jake dit : « I’ll have a mechanic check a few cars this weekend ». Have + personne + verbe : quelqu’un d’autre le fait.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u05-l03-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u05-l03","position":6,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"I had my phone repaired last week.","options":["I had my phone repaired last week.","I repaired my phone last week.","I had my phone repaired last month.","I have my phone repaired every year."]},"answer":"I had my phone repaired last week.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-have-something-done"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u05-l03-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u05-l03","position":7,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Remets les mots dans l’ordre","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["I","would","like","to","have","the","screen","replaced"],"translation":"J’aimerais faire remplacer l’écran."},"answer":"I would like to have the screen replaced.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["efr-have-something-done","efr-replace"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u05-l03-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u05-l03","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Réponds en anglais","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Your hair looks great! Did you cut it yourself? (non, tu te les es fait couper chez le coiffeur)","translation":"Tes cheveux sont super ! Tu les as coupés toi-même ?"},"answer":"No, I had it cut at the hairdresser.","accepted_answers":["No, I had it cut at the hairdresser's.","No, I got it cut at the hairdresser.","No, I had it cut."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-have-something-done"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u05-l03-e09","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u05-l03","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"La semaine dernière, j’ai fait réparer mon téléphone."},"answer":"I had my phone repaired last week.","accepted_answers":["I got my phone repaired last week.","Last week I had my phone repaired.","I had my phone fixed last week.","I got my phone fixed last week."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-have-something-done"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u05-l04-e01","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u05-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Associe chaque mot à sa signification","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"by far","right":"de loin / largement"},{"left":"twice as","right":"deux fois plus / deux fois autant"},{"left":"nowhere near","right":"loin d’être / loin de là"},{"left":"value for money","right":"bon rapport qualité-prix"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-by-far","efr-twice-as","efr-nowhere-near","efr-value-for-money"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u05-l04-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u05-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"This phone is twice as expensive ___ that one.","translation":"Ce téléphone est deux fois plus cher que celui-là.","options":["as","than","like","that"]},"answer":"as","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Twice as + adjectif + as (pas than, même si on dit « deux fois plus… que »).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-twice-as"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u05-l04-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u05-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"It was by ___ the best decision I made.","translation":"C’était de loin la meilleure décision que j’ai prise.","options":["far","much","long","more"]},"answer":"far","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-by-far"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u05-l04-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u05-l04","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The ___ the phone, the less sense it makes.","translation":"Plus le téléphone est vieux, moins ça a de sens.","options":["older","old","oldest","more old"]},"answer":"older","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"The + comparatif, the + comparatif : plus…, plus…","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-twice-as"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u05-l04-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u05-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u5-repair","setting":"Un client dans une boutique de réparation de téléphones.","speakers":[{"name":"Customer","voice":"a"},{"name":"Assistant","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Customer","text":"Hi. I dropped my phone yesterday and I'd like to have the screen replaced."},{"speaker":"Assistant","text":"Let me see. Yes, we can do that. It's ninety dollars, and it'll be ready tomorrow."},{"speaker":"Customer","text":"Ninety? That's twice as much as I paid last time!"},{"speaker":"Assistant","text":"Last time you had a cheaper screen put in. This one is original. The cheaper ones are nowhere near as good."},{"speaker":"Customer","text":"Hmm. Is it worth it? The phone is three years old."},{"speaker":"Assistant","text":"Honestly, the older the phone, the less sense it makes. A new one costs about four hundred."},{"speaker":"Customer","text":"I can't afford a new one right now. Go ahead and replace the screen, please."}]},"question":"Pourquoi l’écran coûte-t-il deux fois plus cher cette fois ?","options":["Parce qu’il est d’origine ; la dernière fois, on lui en a mis un moins cher","Parce que le téléphone est neuf","Parce qu’il sera prêt aujourd’hui","Parce que les prix ont augmenté"]},"answer":"Parce qu’il est d’origine ; la dernière fois, on lui en a mis un moins cher","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’employé dit : « Last time you had a cheaper screen put in. This one is original. The cheaper ones are nowhere near as good ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u05-l04-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u05-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u5-savings","document":"post","setting":"Un article de blog sur comment économiser.","title":"How I saved $3,000 in a year","lines":["Last January I looked at my bank account and realized I had no savings at all. So I decided to change a few things.","First, I cut back on subscriptions. I was paying for four streaming services and a gym I never went to. Canceling them saved me sixty dollars a month.","Second, I started buying second-hand clothes and furniture. Most of it is in perfect condition and costs half the price.","Third, before buying anything, I ask myself one question: is this good value for money, or do I just want it?","One year later, I have saved three thousand dollars. It was by far the best decision I made last year."]},"question":"Comment l’autrice juge-t-elle sa décision d’économiser ?","options":["Comme de loin la meilleure décision de l’année dernière","Comme une erreur","Comme quelque chose de difficile qu’elle ne referait pas","Comme une décision parmi d’autres"]},"answer":"Comme de loin la meilleure décision de l’année dernière","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Elle écrit : « It was by far the best decision I made last year ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u05-l04-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u05-l04","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"The cheap ones are nowhere near as good.","options":["The cheap ones are nowhere near as good.","The cheap ones are just as good.","The cheap ones are nowhere near as bad.","The new ones are nowhere near as good."]},"answer":"The cheap ones are nowhere near as good.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-nowhere-near"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u05-l04-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u05-l04","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Remets les mots dans l’ordre","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["This","restaurant","is","great","value","for","money"],"translation":"Ce restaurant a un excellent rapport qualité-prix."},"answer":"This restaurant is gre