ev1","position":6,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"You ___ have joked about her job. She was very nervous.","translation":"Tu n’aurais pas dû plaisanter sur son travail. Elle était très stressée.","options":["shouldn't","can't","must","could"]},"answer":"shouldn't","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-should-have"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-rev1-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-rev1","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"could have","options":["could have","overreact","take it personally","can't have"]},"answer":"could have","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-could-have"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-rev1-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-rev1","position":8,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Que veut dire « must have » ?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"must have","options":["a dû / sûrement (passé)","humeur / état d’esprit","a peut-être / il se peut que… ait","reconnaissant"]},"answer":"a dû / sûrement (passé)","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["efr-must-have"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-rev1-e09","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-rev1","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Tu as dû être très fatigué."},"answer":"You must have been very tired.","accepted_answers":["You must've been very tired.","You must have been really tired."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-must-have"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-rev1-e10","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-rev1","position":10,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"You worked twelve hours. You must have ___ exhausted.","translation":"Tu as travaillé douze heures. Tu as dû être épuisé.","options":["been","be","being","was"]},"answer":"been","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Modal + have + participe : must have been.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-must-have"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l03-e01","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l03","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Associe chaque mot à sa signification","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"fall out","right":"se brouiller / se fâcher (avec quelqu’un)"},{"left":"make up","right":"se réconcilier / faire la paix"},{"left":"overreact","right":"exagérer / réagir de façon excessive"},{"left":"take it personally","right":"le prendre personnellement"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-fall-out","efr-make-up","efr-overreact","efr-take-it-personally"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l03-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I fell ___ with my best friend last week.","translation":"La semaine dernière, je me suis fâchée avec ma meilleure amie.","options":["out","up","down","off"]},"answer":"out","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-fall-out"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l03-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"They argued, but they made ___ the next day.","translation":"Ils se sont disputés, mais ils se sont réconciliés le lendemain.","options":["up","out","down","off"]},"answer":"up","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-make-up"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l03-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l03","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u6-advice","document":"post","setting":"Un courrier des lecteurs : la lettre d’une lectrice et la réponse.","title":"Ask Ruth","lines":["Dear Ruth, Last week I fell out with my best friend. She was an hour late for my birthday dinner, and I shouted at her in front of everyone. Now I feel guilty, but I am also still a bit angry. What should I do? — Lina","Dear Lina, It sounds like you both made mistakes. Being an hour late is rude, and you had every right to be upset. However, you probably overreacted when you shouted at her in public.","Try not to take it personally. She could have had a good reason for being late. Call her, tell her how you felt, and listen to her side of the story.","Friends fall out all the time. What matters is how you make up. — Ruth"]},"question":"Pourquoi Lina et son amie se sont-elles fâchées ?","options":["L’amie est arrivée avec une heure de retard et Lina lui a crié dessus devant tout le monde","L’amie n’est pas venue à l’anniversaire","Lina est arrivée en retard à un dîner","L’amie a crié sur Lina"]},"answer":"L’amie est arrivée avec une heure de retard et Lina lui a crié dessus devant tout le monde","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Lina écrit : « She was an hour late for my birthday dinner, and I shouted at her in front of everyone ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l03-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u6-advice","document":"post","setting":"Un courrier des lecteurs : la lettre d’une lectrice et la réponse.","title":"Ask Ruth","lines":["Dear Ruth, Last week I fell out with my best friend. She was an hour late for my birthday dinner, and I shouted at her in front of everyone. Now I feel guilty, but I am also still a bit angry. What should I do? — Lina","Dear Lina, It sounds like you both made mistakes. Being an hour late is rude, and you had every right to be upset. However, you probably overreacted when you shouted at her in public.","Try not to take it personally. She could have had a good reason for being late. Call her, tell her how you felt, and listen to her side of the story.","Friends fall out all the time. What matters is how you make up. — Ruth"]},"question":"Quel est l’avis de Ruth ?","options":["Elles ont toutes les deux eu tort : arriver en retard était impoli, mais Lina a exagéré","Seule l’amie a eu tort","Seule Lina a eu tort","Aucune n’a eu tort"]},"answer":"Elles ont toutes les deux eu tort : arriver en retard était impoli, mais Lina a exagéré","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ruth répond : « you both made mistakes… you probably overreacted when you shouted at her in public ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l03-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u6-advice","document":"post","setting":"Un courrier des lecteurs : la lettre d’une lectrice et la réponse.","title":"Ask Ruth","lines":["Dear Ruth, Last week I fell out with my best friend. She was an hour late for my birthday dinner, and I shouted at her in front of everyone. Now I feel guilty, but I am also still a bit angry. What should I do? — Lina","Dear Lina, It sounds like you both made mistakes. Being an hour late is rude, and you had every right to be upset. However, you probably overreacted when you shouted at her in public.","Try not to take it personally. She could have had a good reason for being late. Call her, tell her how you felt, and listen to her side of the story.","Friends fall out all the time. What matters is how you make up. — Ruth"]},"question":"Selon Ruth, qu’est-ce qui compte le plus ?","options":["La façon de se réconcilier, parce que les amis se disputent tout le temps","Ne jamais se disputer","Savoir qui a raison","Que l’amie s’excuse en premier"]},"answer":"La façon de se réconcilier, parce que les amis se disputent tout le temps","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ruth conclut : « Friends fall out all the time. What matters is how you make up ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l03-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l03","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Don't take it personally. He is rude to everyone.","options":["Don't take it personally. He is rude to everyone.","Don't take it personally. He is nice to everyone.","Take it personally. He is rude to everyone.","Don't take it personally. She is rude to everyone."]},"answer":"Don't take it personally. He is rude to everyone.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-take-it-personally"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l03-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l03","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Remets les mots dans l’ordre","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["I","am","sorry","I","overreacted","yesterday"],"translation":"Désolé d’avoir exagéré hier."},"answer":"I am sorry I overreacted yesterday.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["efr-overreact"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l03-e09","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l03","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Réponds en anglais","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Are you still angry with your sister? (non, vous vous êtes déjà réconciliés)","translation":"Tu es encore fâché contre ta sœur ?"},"answer":"No, we have made up.","accepted_answers":["No, we've made up.","No, we made up.","No. We have made up."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-make-up"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l03-e10","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Ne le prends pas personnellement."},"answer":"Don't take it personally.","accepted_answers":["Do not take it personally.","Please don't take it personally."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-take-it-personally"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l04-e01","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Associe chaque mot à sa signification","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"mood","right":"humeur / état d’esprit"},{"left":"cheer up","right":"remonter le moral / encourager"},{"left":"let down","right":"décevoir / laisser tomber (quelqu’un)"},{"left":"grateful","right":"reconnaissant"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-mood","efr-cheer-up","efr-let-down","efr-grateful"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l04-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l04","position":2,"type":"image_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Que montre l’image ?","payload":{"type":"image_choice","emoji":"🐂","options":["stubborn","grateful","guilty","upset"]},"answer":"stubborn","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["efr-stubborn"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l04-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Don't talk to him now. He is in a bad ___.","translation":"Ne lui parle pas maintenant. Il est de mauvaise humeur.","options":["mood","tone","day","time"]},"answer":"mood","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Be in a good / bad mood : être de bonne / mauvaise humeur.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-mood"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l04-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l04","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I trusted you, and you let me ___.","translation":"Je t’ai fait confiance, et tu m’as laissé tomber.","options":["down","up","out","off"]},"answer":"down","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-let-down"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l04-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u6-sorry","document":"message","setting":"Un message d’excuses entre amis.","from":"Sara","to":"Max","lines":["Hi Max, I'm sorry I didn't reply. I wasn't angry with you. My first week at the new job was awful, and I was in a terrible mood.","Your joke was a bit much, but I know you didn’t mean it. I was being too sensitive.","I'm really grateful that you called last night. You always know how to cheer me up.","I promise I won't disappear like that again. I hate letting my friends down. Coffee on Saturday? Sara"]},"question":"Pourquoi Sara ne répondait-elle pas aux messages ?","options":["Elle a eu une première semaine horrible au travail et elle était de très mauvaise humeur","Elle était fâchée contre Max","Elle avait perdu son téléphone","Elle était en voyage"]},"answer":"Elle a eu une première semaine horrible au travail et elle était de très mauvaise humeur","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Sara écrit : « I wasn’t angry with you. My first week at the new job was awful, and I was in a terrible mood ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l04-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading",