,"prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Ne le prends pas personnellement."},"answer":"Don't take it personally.","accepted_answers":["Do not take it personally.","Please don't take it personally."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-take-it-personally"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-rev2-e10","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-rev2","position":10,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"They argued, but they made ___ the next day.","translation":"Ils se sont disputés, mais ils se sont réconciliés le lendemain.","options":["up","out","down","off"]},"answer":"up","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-make-up"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l05-e01","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l05","position":1,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Que veut dire « self-confidence » ?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"self-confidence","options":["confiance en soi / assurance","empathie","humeur / état d’esprit","coupable"]},"answer":"confiance en soi / assurance","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["efr-self-confidence"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l05-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l05","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ means understanding how others feel.","translation":"L’empathie, c’est comprendre ce que ressentent les autres.","options":["Empathy","Mood","Self-confidence","Diversity"]},"answer":"Empathy","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-empathy"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l05-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l05","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Learning a language gave me more ___.","translation":"Apprendre une langue m’a donné plus confiance en moi.","options":["self-confidence","empathy","mood","evidence"]},"answer":"self-confidence","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-self-confidence"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l05-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l05","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u6-podcast","setting":"Un podcast de psychologie interviewe un psychologue.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Moss","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"Today we are talking about empathy. What exactly is it?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"It is the ability to understand how another person feels, to put yourself in their shoes. It's not the same as agreeing with them."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Can empathy be learned?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Yes. The first step is to listen without judging. Most of us listen only to answer."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Some listeners say their mood changes very quickly. Is that normal?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Everybody has good and bad days. But if you are often in a bad mood, it might be stress, or a lack of sleep."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And what about self-confidence?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"People with low self-confidence tend to think that others are judging them. Usually, others are too busy thinking about themselves!"}]},"question":"Selon le psychologue, l’empathie, est-ce la même chose qu’être d’accord ?","options":["Non : c’est comprendre ce que ressent l’autre, même si tu n’es pas d’accord","Oui, c’est la même chose","Oui, mais seulement avec les amis","Non : c’est donner des conseils"]},"answer":"Non : c’est comprendre ce que ressent l’autre, même si tu n’es pas d’accord","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Il dit : « It is the ability to understand how another person feels… It’s not the same as agreeing with them ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l05-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l05","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u6-podcast","setting":"Un podcast de psychologie interviewe un psychologue.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Moss","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"Today we are talking about empathy. What exactly is it?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"It is the ability to understand how another person feels, to put yourself in their shoes. It's not the same as agreeing with them."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Can empathy be learned?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Yes. The first step is to listen without judging. Most of us listen only to answer."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Some listeners say their mood changes very quickly. Is that normal?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Everybody has good and bad days. But if you are often in a bad mood, it might be stress, or a lack of sleep."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And what about self-confidence?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"People with low self-confidence tend to think that others are judging them. Usually, others are too busy thinking about themselves!"}]},"question":"Qu’est-ce qui peut expliquer qu’on soit souvent de mauvaise humeur ?","options":["Le stress ou le manque de sommeil","Une mauvaise alimentation","Trop de travail en équipe","La météo"]},"answer":"Le stress ou le manque de sommeil","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Il dit : « if you are often in a bad mood, it might be stress, or a lack of sleep ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l05-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l05","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u6-podcast","setting":"Un podcast de psychologie interviewe un psychologue.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Moss","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"Today we are talking about empathy. What exactly is it?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"It is the ability to understand how another person feels, to put yourself in their shoes. It's not the same as agreeing with them."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Can empathy be learned?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Yes. The first step is to listen without judging. Most of us listen only to answer."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Some listeners say their mood changes very quickly. Is that normal?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Everybody has good and bad days. But if you are often in a bad mood, it might be stress, or a lack of sleep."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And what about self-confidence?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"People with low self-confidence tend to think that others are judging them. Usually, others are too busy thinking about themselves!"}]},"question":"Que dit-il avec humour sur les personnes qui manquent de confiance en elles ?","options":["Elles croient que les autres les jugent, mais les autres pensent à eux-mêmes","Qu’elles ne changent jamais","Qu’elles ont raison","Qu’elles devraient parler plus"]},"answer":"Elles croient que les autres les jugent, mais les autres pensent à eux-mêmes","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Il dit : « People with low self-confidence tend to think that others are judging them. Usually, others are too busy thinking about themselves! ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u06-l05-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u06-l05","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Empathy means understanding how others feel.","options":["Empathy means understanding how others feel.