r","voice":"a"},{"name":"Paula","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"We go now to Paula, who is in the south, where there hasn't been any real rain for eight months."},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Thanks. This is the worst drought in fifty years. Despite the storms last week, the rivers are still very low."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"How are farmers dealing with it?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"With great difficulty. Even though they have reduced their water use, many have lost half of their crops. And there is now a water shortage in three towns."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"Is this connected to global warming?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Scientists say yes. Ironically, two years ago this same region suffered terrible floods. Extreme weather, in both directions, is a direct consequence of a warmer planet."}]},"question":"Pourquoi les rivières sont-elles toujours basses ?","options":["Parce que les orages de la semaine dernière n’ont pas suffi après huit mois sans pluie","Parce que les agriculteurs utilisent trop d’eau","Parce qu’il y a eu des inondations","Parce qu’on a fermé un barrage"]},"answer":"Parce que les orages de la semaine dernière n’ont pas suffi après huit mois sans pluie","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Paula dit : « This is the worst drought in fifty years. Despite the storms last week, the rivers are still very low ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l02-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l02","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u7-drought","setting":"Un reportage radio sur la sécheresse dans une région agricole.","speakers":[{"name":"Presenter","voice":"a"},{"name":"Paula","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"We go now to Paula, who is in the south, where there hasn't been any real rain for eight months."},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Thanks. This is the worst drought in fifty years. Despite the storms last week, the rivers are still very low."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"How are farmers dealing with it?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"With great difficulty. Even though they have reduced their water use, many have lost half of their crops. And there is now a water shortage in three towns."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"Is this connected to global warming?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Scientists say yes. Ironically, two years ago this same region suffered terrible floods. Extreme weather, in both directions, is a direct consequence of a warmer planet."}]},"question":"Qu’est-ce que la situation a d’ironique, selon Paula ?","options":["Qu’il y a deux ans, la même région a subi de terribles inondations","Qu’il n’avait jamais autant plu","Que les agriculteurs ont gagné plus","Que les scientifiques ne connaissent pas la cause"]},"answer":"Qu’il y a deux ans, la même région a subi de terribles inondations","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Paula dit : « Ironically, two years ago this same region suffered terrible floods ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l02-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l02","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u7-report","document":"notice","setting":"Le résumé du rapport d’une organisation environnementale.","title":"Our planet: 2026 report","lines":["Key findings of our annual report:","More than one million species are endangered, mainly because of the loss of forests and the pollution of oceans.","Climate change is a growing threat not only to nature, but to people. Floods and droughts hit the poorest countries hardest, even though they produce the lowest emissions.","Poverty and the environment are connected: when people are poor, they often have no choice but to cut down forests to survive.","Despite these problems, there is good news. Several species have been saved in the last ten years, which shows that action works."]},"question":"Qui est le plus touché par les sécheresses et les inondations, selon le rapport ?","options":["Les pays les plus pauvres, alors que ce sont eux qui polluent le moins","Les pays les plus riches","Les grandes entreprises","Tout le monde de la même façon"]},"answer":"Les pays les plus pauvres, alors que ce sont eux qui polluent le moins","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Le rapport dit : « Floods and droughts hit the poorest countries hardest, even though they produce the lowest emissions ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l02-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l02","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"The flood destroyed many homes.","options":["The flood destroyed many homes.","The flood destroyed many roads.","The storm destroyed many homes.","The floods destroyed a few homes."]},"answer":"The flood destroyed many homes.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-flood"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l02-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l02","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Réponds en anglais","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Why is there no water in the town? (à cause de la sécheresse)","translation":"Pourquoi n’y a-t-il pas d’eau au village ?"},"answer":"Because of the drought.","accepted_answers":["Because there is a drought.","It's because of the drought.","Because of the drought, there is no water."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-drought"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l02-e09","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l02","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"C’est la pire sécheresse depuis cinquante ans."},"answer":"It is the worst drought in fifty years.","accepted_answers":["It's the worst drought in fifty years.","This is the worst drought in fifty years.","It is the worst drought in 50 years."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-drought"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1-e01","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1","position":1,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"shortage","options":["shortage","poverty","global warming","sustainable"]},"answer":"shortage","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-shortage"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1","position":2,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Remets les mots dans l’ordre","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Cars","produce","a","lot","of","emissions"],"translation":"Les voitures produisent beaucoup d’émissions."},"answer":"Cars produce a lot of emissions.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["efr-emissions"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1","position":3,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Que veut dire « flood » ?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"flood","options":["inondation","réchauffement climatique","menace","pénurie / manque"]},"answer":"inondation","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["efr-flood"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1","position":4,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Que veut dire « global warming » ?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"global warming","options":["réchauffement climatique","s’attaquer à (un problème)","bien que / même si (fait réel)","sécheresse"]},"answer":"réchauffement climatique","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["efr-global-warming"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1","position":5,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"C’est la pire sécheresse depuis cinquante ans."},"answer":"It is the worst drought in fifty years.","accepted_answers":["It's the worst drought in fifty years.","This is the worst drought in fifty years.","It is the worst drought in 50 years."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-drought"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1","position":6,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Associe chaque mot à sa signification","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"drought","right":"sécheresse"},{"left":"global warming","right":"réchauffement climatique"},{"left":"shortage","right":"pénurie / manque"},{"left":"threat","right":"menace"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-drought","efr-global-warming","efr-shortage","efr-threat"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1","position":7,"type":"complete_word","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Écris le mot en entier","payload":{"type":"complete_word","masked":"t_r_a_","hint":"menace"},"answer":"threat","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":20,"words":["efr-threat"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1","position":8,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Eating less meat reduces your carbon ___.","translation":"Manger moins de viande réduit ton empreinte carbone.","options":["footprint","step","warming","size"]},"answer":"footprint","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-carbon-footprint"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1-e09","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1","position":9,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Que veut dire « drought » ?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"drought","options":["sécheresse","conséquence","réchauffement climatique","menace"]},"answer":"sécheresse","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["efr-drought"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1-e10","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-rev1","position":10,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Réponds en anglais","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Why is there no water in the town? (à cause de la sécheresse)","translation":"Pourquoi n’y a-t-il pas d’eau au village ?"},"answer":"Because of the drought.","accepted_answers":["Because there is a drought.","It's because of the drought.","Because of the drought, there is no water."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-drought"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l03-e01","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l03","position":1,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ the rain, we went for a walk.","translation":"Malgré la pluie, nous sommes allés nous promener.","options":["Despite","Even though","Although","Even if"]},"answer":"Despite","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Despite + nom (the rain). Even though et although sont suivis d’une proposition.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-despite"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l03-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ I was tired, I finished the report.","translation":"Même si j’étais fatigué, j’ai fini le rapport.","options":["Even though","Despite","In spite of","Whereas"]},"answer":"Even though","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Even though + proposition complète (I was tired).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-even-though"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l03-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"In spite ___ the price, I take the train.","translation":"En dépit du prix, je prends le train.","options":["of","to","for","that"]},"answer":"of","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"In spite of (avec of) ; despite s’emploie sans of, comme « malgré ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-in-spite-of","efr-tackle","efr-sustainable"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l03-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l03","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ it rains, the game will go ahead.","translation":"Même s’il pleut, le match aura lieu.","options":["Even if","Despite","Whereas","In spite of"]},"answer":"Even if","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-even-if"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l03-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u7-students","setting":"Deux étudiants débattent : une seule personne peut-elle aider la planète ?","speakers":[{"name":"Noah","voice":"a"},{"name":"Mia","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I've stopped flying. In spite of the price, I take the train to visit my family."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"That's great, but honestly, it won't change anything. Even if everyone in this city stopped flying, it would be a tiny difference."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I don't agree. Big changes always start with small groups of people."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"Maybe. But we need to tackle the real causes: coal, oil, and the way we produce food."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"Sure, but those things change when people demand something different."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"OK, that's a fair point. So we both want a sustainable future. We just disagree about how to get there."}]},"question":"Que fait Noah malgré le prix ?","options":["Il prend le train pour aller voir sa famille au lieu de prendre l’avion","Il prend moins l’avion pendant les vacances","Il va à la fac à vélo","Il a arrêté de manger de la viande"]},"answer":"Il prend le train pour aller voir sa famille au lieu de prendre l’avion","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Noah dit : « I’ve stopped flying. In spite of the price, I take the train to visit my family ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l03-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u7-students","setting":"Deux étudiants débattent : une seule personne peut-elle aider la planète ?","speakers":[{"name":"Noah","voice":"a"},{"name":"Mia","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I've stopped flying. In spite of the price, I take the train to visit my family."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"That's great, but honestly, it won't change anything. Even if everyone in this city stopped flying, it would be a tiny difference."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I don't agree. Big changes always start with small groups of people."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"Maybe. But we need to tackle the real causes: coal, oil, and the way we produce food."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"Sure, but those things change when people demand something different."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"OK, that's a fair point. So we both want a sustainable future. We just disagree about how to get there."}]},"question":"Que veut dire Mia avec « Even if everyone in this city stopped flying, it would be a tiny difference » ?","options":["Que même si tout le monde le faisait, l’effet serait très faible","Que personne n’arrêtera de prendre l’avion","Que l’avion ne pollue pas","Que la ville est très petite"]},"answer":"Que même si tout le monde le faisait, l’effet serait très faible","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Even if : même si tout le monde arrêtait de prendre l’avion, le résultat (une différence minime) ne changerait pas.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l03-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l03","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u7-drought","setting":"Un reportage radio sur la sécheresse dans une région agricole.","speakers":[{"name":"Presenter","voice":"a"},{"name":"Paula","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"We go now to Paula, who is in the south, where there hasn't been any real rain for eight months."},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Thanks. This is the worst drought in fifty years. Despite the storms last week, the rivers are still very low."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"How are farmers dealing with it?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"With great difficulty. Even though they have reduced their water use, many have lost half of their crops. And there is now a water shortage in three towns."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"Is this connected to global warming?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Scientists say yes. Ironically, two years ago this same region suffered terrible floods. Extreme weather, in both directions, is a direct consequence of a warmer planet."}]},"question":"Qu’est-il arrivé aux agriculteurs bien qu’ils aient réduit leur consommation d’eau ?","options":["Beaucoup ont perdu la moitié de leurs récoltes","Ils ont gagné plus d’argent","Ils ont déménagé dans une autre région","Ils n’ont eu aucun problème"]},"answer":"Beaucoup ont perdu la moitié de leurs récoltes","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Paula dit : « Even though they have reduced their water use, many have lost half of their crops ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l03-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l03","position":8,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Even though I was tired, I finished the report.","options":["Even though I was tired, I finished the report.","Because I was tired, I finished the report.","Even though I was tired, I started the report.","Even though I was busy, I finished the report."]},"answer":"Even though I was tired, I finished the report.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-even-though"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l03-e09","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l03","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Réponds en anglais","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Did you go to the beach? (oui, malgré le froid)","translation":"Vous êtes allés à la plage ?"},"answer":"Yes, despite the cold.","accepted_answers":["Yes, in spite of the cold.","Yes, we went despite the cold.","Yes, even though it was cold."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-despite"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l03-e10","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Malgré la pluie, nous sommes allés nous promener."},"answer":"Despite the rain, we went for a walk.","accepted_answers":["In spite of the rain, we went for a walk.","Despite the rain we went for a walk.","We went for a walk despite the rain."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-despite"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l04-e01","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Associe chaque mot à sa signification","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"renewable","right":"renouvelable"},{"left":"sustainable","right":"durable"},{"left":"tackle","right":"s’attaquer à (un problème)"},{"left":"whereas","right":"alors que / tandis que"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-renewable","efr-sustainable","efr-tackle","efr-whereas"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l04-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I love the city, ___ my brother prefers the country.","translation":"Moi, j’adore la ville, alors que mon frère préfère la campagne.","options":["whereas","despite","even if","in spite of"]},"answer":"whereas","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Whereas relie deux faits opposés.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-whereas"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l04-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"We need to ___ the real causes of the problem.","translation":"Nous devons nous attaquer aux vraies causes du problème.","options":["tackle","reduce","produce","protect"]},"answer":"tackle","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Collocation : tackle a problem (s’attaquer à un problème).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-tackle"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l04-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l04","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u7-footprint","document":"post","setting":"Une tribune sur l’empreinte carbone.","title":"Your shower will not save the planet","lines":["We are constantly told to reduce our carbon footprint: take shorter showers, eat less meat, fly less. These things matter, but they are not enough.","Just one hundred companies are responsible for most of the world’s emissions. Whereas a single family can save a few tons of CO2 a year, one large factory can produce millions.","This does not mean that individual action is useless. Even if your own impact is small, your choices send a message to companies and governments.","The real solution is a fast move to renewable energy, such as solar and wind. Only governments can make that happen, and only if we vote for it."]},"question":"Quelle est la vraie solution, selon l’auteur ?","options":["Passer vite aux énergies renouvelables, ce que seuls les gouvernements peuvent faire","Que chaque famille prenne des douches courtes","Fermer toutes les usines","Arrêter de voter"]},"answer":"Passer vite aux énergies renouvelables, ce que seuls les gouvernements peuvent faire","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’article dit : « The real solution is a fast move to renewable energy… Only governments can make that happen ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l04-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u7-students","setting":"Deux étudiants débattent : une seule personne peut-elle aider la planète ?","speakers":[{"name":"Noah","voice":"a"},{"name":"Mia","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I've stopped flying. In spite of the price, I take the train to visit my family."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"That's great, but honestly, it won't change anything. Even if everyone in this city stopped flying, it would be a tiny difference."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I don't agree. Big changes always start with small groups of people."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"Maybe. But we need to tackle the real causes: coal, oil, and the way we produce food."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"Sure, but those things change when people demand something different."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"OK, that's a fair point. So we both want a sustainable future. We just disagree about how to get there."}]},"question":"Sur quoi Noah et Mia finissent-ils par être d’accord ?","options":["Ils veulent tous les deux un avenir durable, mais pas de la même façon","Ils vont tous les deux arrêter de prendre l’avion","Ils ne sont d’accord sur rien","Mia admet qu’une seule personne peut tout changer"]},"answer":"Ils veulent tous les deux un avenir durable, mais pas de la même façon","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Mia dit : « So we both want a sustainable future. We just disagree about how to get there ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u07-l04-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u07-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u7-students","setting":"Deux étudiants débattent : une seule personne peut-elle aider la planète ?","speakers":[{"name":"Noah","voice":"a"},{"name":"Mia","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I've stopped flying. In spite of the price, I take the train to visit my family."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"That's great, but honestly, it won't change anything. Even if everyone in this city stopped flying, it would be a tiny difference."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I don't agree. Big changes always start with small groups of people."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"Maybe. But we need to tackle the real causes: coal, oil, and the way we produce food."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"Sure, but those things change when people demand something different."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"OK, that's a fair point. So we both want a sustainable future. We just disagree about how to get there."}]},"question":"À quelles causes Mia veut-elle s’attaquer ?","options":["Le charbon, le pétrole et notre façon de produi