ranslation":"La vidéo est devenue virale en un jour.","options":["went","made","did","got"]},"answer":"went","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Go viral (went viral) : devenir viral.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-go-viral"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l01-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l01","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Fake news ___ faster than the truth.","translation":"Les fausses nouvelles se répandent plus vite que la vérité.","options":["spreads","spread","spreading","is spread"]},"answer":"spreads","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"News est au singulier en anglais (contrairement à « les nouvelles ») : news spreads.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-spread"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l01-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l01","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u8-viral","setting":"Deux amies parlent d’une publication devenue virale.","speakers":[{"name":"Zoe","voice":"a"},{"name":"Amy","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Zoe","text":"Have you seen this? A post says that drinking hot water every hour stops you from getting a cold."},{"speaker":"Amy","text":"I've seen it. It went viral yesterday. My aunt has already shared it with the whole family."},{"speaker":"Zoe","text":"Is it true, though? The post claims that doctors recommend it."},{"speaker":"Amy","text":"Which doctors? It doesn’t say. That’s how misinformation spreads: no names, no sources, just a big promise."},{"speaker":"Zoe","text":"So it’s just a rumor?"},{"speaker":"Amy","text":"Probably. A fact-checking website looked at it this morning. They found no evidence at all."},{"speaker":"Zoe","text":"I'll send the link to your aunt, then. Before she shares the next one!"}]},"question":"Que dit la publication virale ?","options":["