,"right":"refuser de"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-accuse","efr-deny","efr-admit","efr-refuse"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l03-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"They accused him ___ lying.","translation":"Ils l’ont accusé de mentir.","options":["of","for","to","about"]},"answer":"of","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Accuse someone of + -ing.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-accuse"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l03-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"He denied ___ the money.","translation":"Il a nié avoir pris l’argent.","options":["taking","to take","take","took"]},"answer":"taking","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Deny + -ing.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-deny"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l03-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l03","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"He refused ___ the question.","translation":"Il a refusé de répondre à la question.","options":["to answer","answering","answer","of answering"]},"answer":"to answer","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Refuse to + verbe.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-refuse"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l03-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u8-interview","setting":"Une interview télévisée d’un homme politique.","speakers":[{"name":"Journalist","voice":"a"},{"name":"Hart","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Mr. Hart, a newspaper has accused your party of using public money for its campaign. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I completely deny that. Every dollar we spent was ours."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"But you admitted last week that the campaign had used government offices."},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I admitted using one office for one meeting. That's very different."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Will you publish the campaign accounts?"},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I refuse to answer questions based on rumors. I insist that we haven't done anything wrong."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Many viewers will find that answer hard to believe."}]},"question":"De quoi un journal a-t-il accusé le parti de Hart ?","options":["D’utiliser de l’argent public pour sa campagne","D’avoir menti dans une interview","D’avoir fermé des bureaux du gouvernement","De ne pas payer d’impôts"]},"answer":"D’utiliser de l’argent public pour sa campagne","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"La journaliste dit : « a newspaper has accused your party of using public money for its campaign ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l03-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u8-interview","setting":"Une interview télévisée d’un homme politique.","speakers":[{"name":"Journalist","voice":"a"},{"name":"Hart","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Mr. Hart, a newspaper has accused your party of using public money for its campaign. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I completely deny that. Every dollar we spent was ours."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"But you admitted last week that the campaign had used government offices."},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I admitted using one office for one meeting. That's very different."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Will you publish the campaign accounts?"},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I refuse to answer questions based on rumors. I insist that we haven't done anything wrong."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Many viewers will find that answer hard to believe."}]},"question":"Qu’a admis Hart la semaine précédente, selon lui ?","options":["Avoir utilisé un bureau pour une réunion","Avoir utilisé de l’argent public","Avoir menti","Rien"]},"answer":"Avoir utilisé un bureau pour une réunion","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Hart dit : « I admitted using one office for one meeting. That’s very different ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l03-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l03","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u8-interview","setting":"Une interview télévisée d’un homme politique.","speakers":[{"name":"Journalist","voice":"a"},{"name":"Hart","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Mr. Hart, a newspaper has accused your party of using public money for its campaign. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I completely deny that. Every dollar we spent was ours."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"But you admitted last week that the campaign had used government offices."},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I admitted using one office for one meeting. That's very different."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Will you publish the campaign accounts?"},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I refuse to answer questions based on rumors. I insist that we haven't done anything wrong."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Many viewers will find that answer hard to believe."}]},"question":"Que fait Hart quand on l’interroge sur les comptes de la campagne ?","options":["Il refuse de répondre et dit que ce sont des rumeurs","Il promet de les publier","Il admet qu’il y a eu des erreurs","Il accuse la journaliste"]},"answer":"Il refuse de répondre et dit que ce sont des rumeurs","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Hart dit : « I refuse to answer questions based on rumors. I insist that we haven’t done anything wrong ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l03-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l03","position":8,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"She admitted making a mistake.","options":["She admitted making a mistake.","She denied making a mistake.","She admitted making a promise.","He admitted making a mistake."]},"answer":"She admitted making a mistake.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-admit"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l03-e09","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l03","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Réponds en anglais","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Did he say he took the money? (non, il a nié l’avoir pris)","translation":"Il a dit qu’il avait pris l’argent ?"},"answer":"No, he denied taking it.","accepted_answers":["No, he denied taking the money.","He denied taking it.","No. He denied taking it."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-deny"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l03-e10","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Ils l’ont accusé de mentir."},"answer":"They accused him of lying.","accepted_answers":["He was accused of lying.","They accused him of telling lies."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-accuse"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l04-e01","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Associe chaque mot à sa signification","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"reliable","right":"fiable"},{"left":"biased","right":"partial / biaisé"},{"left":"misleading","right":"trompeur"},{"left":"fact-check","right":"vérifier (les faits)"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-reliable","efr-biased","efr-misleading","efr-fact-check"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l04-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The article is ___. It only shows one side.","translation":"L’article est partial. Il ne montre qu’un seul côté.","options":["biased","reliable","viral","official"]},"answer":"biased","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-biased"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l04-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"That headline is ___. The article says nothing new.","translation":"Ce titre, c’est un piège à clics. L’article ne dit rien de nouveau.","options":["clickbait","reliable","misinformation","rumor"]},"answer":"clickbait","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-clickbait"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l04-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l04","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u8-guide","document":"post","setting":"Un guide pour repérer les fausses informations.","title":"Think before you share","lines":["Five questions to ask before you share a story","1. Who wrote it? Reliable sources tell you who the journalist is and where the information comes from.","2. Does the headline match the story? Clickbait headlines promise something shocking to make you click, but the article often says something different.","3. Is it one-sided? A biased article only shows one side and ignores facts that do not support its argument.","4. Are the numbers misleading? A \"300% rise\" sounds huge, but it may mean the number went from one to four.","5. Have other media reported it? If nobody else has the story, be careful. Check it on a fact-checking site."]},"question":"Selon le guide, que font les titres clickbait ?","options":["Ils promettent quelque chose de choquant pour te faire cliquer, mais l’article dit autre chose","Ils résument bien l’article","Ils donnent le nom du journaliste","Ils montrent les deux côtés"]},"answer":"Ils promettent quelque chose de choquant pour te faire cliquer, mais l’article dit autre chose","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Le guide dit : « Clickbait headlines promise something shocking to make you click, but the article often says something different ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l04-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u8-guide","document":"post","setting":"Un guide pour repérer les fausses informations.","title":"Think before you share","lines":["Five questions to ask before you share a story","1. Who wrote it? Reliable sources tell you who the journalist is and where the information comes from.","2. Does the headline match the story? Clickbait headlines promise something shocking to make you click, but the article often says something different.","3. Is it one-sided? A biased article only shows one side and ignores facts that do not support its argument.","4. Are the numbers misleading? A \"300% rise\" sounds huge, but it may mean the number went from one to four.","5. Have other media reported it? If nobody else has the story, be careful. Check it on a fact-checking site."]},"question":"Pourquoi une « hausse de 300 % » peut-elle être trompeuse ?","options":["Parce que ça peut vouloir dire que le chiffre est passé de un à quatre","Parce que c’est toujours faux","Parce que c’est un tout petit chiffre","Parce que personne ne le vérifie"]},"answer":"Parce que ça peut vouloir dire que le chiffre est passé de un à quatre","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Le guide dit : « A \"300% rise\" sounds huge, but it may mean the number went from one to four ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l04-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u8-guide","document":"post","setting":"Un guide pour repérer les fausses informations.","title":"Think before you share","lines":["Five questions to ask before you share a story","1. Who wrote it? Reliable sources tell you who the journalist is and where the information comes from.","2. Does the headline match the story? Clickbait headlines promise something shocking to make you click, but the article often says something different.","3. Is it one-sided? A biased article only shows one side and ignores facts that do not support its argument.","4. Are the numbers misleading? A \"300% rise\" sounds huge, but it may mean the number went from one to four.","5. Have other media reported it? If nobody else has the story, be careful. Check it on a fact-checking site."]},"question":"Que conseille le guide si aucun autre média n’a publié l’info ?","options":["Être prudent et la vérifier sur un site de vérification","La partager vite","Y croire quand même","Écrire au journaliste"]},"answer":"Être prudent et la vérifier sur un site de vérification","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Le guide dit : « If nobody else has the story, be careful. Check it on a fact-checking site ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u08-l04-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u08-l04","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que