"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l01-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l01","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The plan is cheap. ___, it is easy to start.","translation":"Le plan est bon marché. De plus, il est facile à lancer.","options":["Moreover","However","Although","Unless"]},"answer":"Moreover","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Moreover ajoute une raison dans le même sens ; however marque un contraste.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-moreover"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l01-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l01","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"It rained all week. As a ___, the match was canceled.","translation":"Il a plu toute la semaine. Par conséquent, le match a été annulé.","options":["result","reason","end","point"]},"answer":"result","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-as-a-result"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l01-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l01","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-school-debate","setting":"Un débat au lycée : faut-il interdire les téléphones en classe ?","speakers":[{"name":"Moderator","voice":"a"},{"name":"Lucas","voice":"b"},{"name":"Hannah","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Today's debate: should phones be banned in schools? Lucas, you're first."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"Yes, they should. Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school. As a result, many students feel anxious all day."},{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Hannah, your answer?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"But that's an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Fair question. What I'm saying is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"Quelles raisons Lucas donne-t-il pour interdire les téléphones ?","options":["Ils distraient et facilitent le harcèlement, qui continue après les cours","Ils coûtent cher","Ils se cassent facilement","Les profs ne savent pas s’en servir"]},"answer":"Ils distraient et facilitent le harcèlement, qui continue après les cours","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Lucas dit : « Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l01-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l01","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-school-debate","setting":"Un débat au lycée : faut-il interdire les téléphones en classe ?","speakers":[{"name":"Moderator","voice":"a"},{"name":"Lucas","voice":"b"},{"name":"Hannah","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Today's debate: should phones be banned in schools? Lucas, you're first."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"Yes, they should. Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school. As a result, many students feel anxious all day."},{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Hannah, your answer?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"But that's an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Fair question. What I'm saying is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"Quelle conséquence Lucas mentionne-t-il ?","options":["Beaucoup d’élèves se sentent anxieux toute la journée","Les élèves ont de mauvaises notes","Les parents se plaignent","L’établissement dépense plus"]},"answer":"Beaucoup d’élèves se sentent anxieux toute la journée","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Lucas dit : « As a result, many students feel anxious all day ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l01-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l01","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-free-uni","document":"post","setting":"Une tribune sur l’université gratuite.","title":"Education is an investment, not a cost","lines":["Should university be free? I believe it should.","First, education benefits everyone, not only the student. Educated citizens earn more, pay more taxes and are healthier. Furthermore, free education gives poor students the same chances as rich ones.","Admittedly, free universities cost the government a lot of money, and some people argue that students should pay for their own future. Nevertheless, the long-term benefits outweigh the costs.","It is not the cost of education that should worry us, but the cost of ignorance.","To sum up, free university is not a gift. It is an investment in all of us."]},"question":"Quel deuxième argument l’autrice ajoute-t-elle avec furthermore ?","options":["Que l’éducation gratuite donne aux étudiants pauvres les mêmes chances","Que les diplômés paient moins d’impôts","Que les universités sont bon marché","Que les riches ne devraient pas faire d’études"]},"answer":"Que l’éducation gratuite donne aux étudiants pauvres les mêmes chances","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’article dit : « Furthermore, free education gives poor students the same chances as rich ones ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l01-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l01","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"We had a debate about social media.","options":["We had a debate about social media.","We had a debate about the news.","We have a debate about social media.","They had a debate about social media."]},"answer":"We had a debate about social media.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-debate"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l01-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l01","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Remets les mots dans l’ordre","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Furthermore","free","education","gives","everyone","the","same","chances"],"translation":"Par ailleurs, l’éducation gratuite donne à tous les mêmes chances."},"answer":"Furthermore free education gives everyone the same chances.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["efr-furthermore"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l01-e09","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l01","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Réponds en anglais","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"The match was canceled. Why? (il a plu toute la semaine ; par conséquent, il a été annulé)","translation":"Le match a été annulé. Pourquoi ?"},"answer":"It rained all week. As a result, it was canceled.","accepted_answers":["It rained all week. As a result, the match was canceled.","It rained all week and as a result it was canceled.","It rained all week, as a result it was canceled."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-as-a-result"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l01-e10","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l01","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Le plan est bon marché. De plus, il est facile à lancer."},"answer":"The plan is cheap. Moreover, it is easy to start.","accepted_answers":["The plan is cheap. Moreover, it's easy to start.","The plan is cheap. Furthermore, it is easy to start.","The plan is cheap. Moreover it is easy to start."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-moreover"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l02-e01","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l02","position":1,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ matters is that you tried.","translation":"Ce qui compte, c’est que tu aies essayé.","options":["What","That","Which","It"]},"answer":"What","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"What… is : « ce qui…, c’est… ». On ne dit pas « That matters is ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-what-matters-is"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l02-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l02","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The reason ___ I called is that I need your help.","translation":"La raison pour laquelle j’ai appelé, c’est que j’ai besoin de ton aide.","options":["why","because","what","for"]},"answer":"why","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"The reason why… is that… (pas « is because » dans un registre soutenu).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-the-reason-why"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l02-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l02","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"He was late again. In other ___, he does not care.","translation":"Il est encore arrivé en retard. Autrement dit, ça lui est égal.","options":["words","ways","reasons","times"]},"answer":"words","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-in-other-words"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l02-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l02","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-four-days","setting":"Des collègues discutent de la proposition de travailler quatre jours par semaine.","speakers":[{"name":"Olivia","voice":"a"},{"name":"Ken","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"So, the four-day week. What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays?"},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"We'd take turns. The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they're rested."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"That may be true for some jobs. But we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day."},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"That's a valid point. So let's try it for three months and measure the results."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"OK, I find that convincing. All things considered, a trial is a good compromise."}]},"question":"Qu’est-ce qui inquiète Olivia dans la semaine de quatre jours ?","options":["Qui va s’occuper des clients le vendredi","Gagner moins","Travailler plus d’heures","Que Ken ne soit pas là"]},"answer":"Qui va s’occuper des clients le vendredi","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Olivia dit : « What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays? ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l02-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l02","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-four-days","setting":"Des collègues discutent de la proposition de travailler quatre jours par semaine.","speakers":[{"name":"Olivia","voice":"a"},{"name":"Ken","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"So, the four-day week. What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays?"},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"We'd take turns. The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they're rested."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"That may be true for some jobs. But we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day."},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"That's a valid point. So let's try it for three months and measure the results."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"OK, I find that convincing. All things considered, a trial is a good compromise."}]},"question":"D’après Ken, pourquoi d’autres entreprises sont-elles passées à la semaine de quatre jours ?","options":["Parce que les gens travaillent mieux quand ils sont reposés","Parce qu’elles économisent de l’argent","Parce que les clients l’ont demandé","Parce que c’est la loi"]},"answer":"Parce que les gens travaillent mieux quand ils sont reposés","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ken dit : « The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they’re rested ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l02-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l02","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-school-debate","setting":"Un débat au lycée : faut-il interdire les téléphones en classe ?","speakers":[{"name":"Moderator","voice":"a"},{"name":"Lucas","voice":"b"},{"name":"Hannah","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Today's debate: should phones be banned in schools? Lucas, you're first."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"Yes, they should. Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school. As a result, many students feel anxious all day."},{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Hannah, your answer?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"But that's an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Fair question. What I'm saying is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"Que précise Hannah avec « In other words… » ?","options":["Qu’avec l’interdiction, les élèves vont juste se servir davantage de leur téléphone à la maison","Que les téléphones sont dangereux","Qu’elle est d’accord avec Lucas","Qu’elle n’a pas de preuves"]},"answer":"Qu’avec l’interdiction, les élèves vont juste se servir davantage de leur téléphone à la maison","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Hannah dit : « a ban doesn’t teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l02-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l02","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"What matters is that you tried.","options":["What matters is that you tried.","What matters is that you won.","It doesn't matter that you tried.","What matters is that we tried."]},"answer":"What matters is that you tried.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-what-matters-is"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l02-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l02","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Remets les mots dans l’ordre","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["What","worries","me","is","the","cost"],"translation":"Ce qui m’inquiète, c’est le coût."},"answer":"What worries me is the cost.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["efr-what-matters-is"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l02-e09","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l02","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Réponds en anglais","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Why are you studying English? (la raison, c’est que tu veux travailler à l’étranger)","translation":"Pourquoi est-ce que tu étudies l’anglais ?"},"answer":"The reason why I am studying English is that I want to work abroad.","accepted_answers":["The reason why I'm studying English is that I want to work abroad.","The reason is that I want to work abroad.","The reason why is that I want to work abroad."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-the-reason-why"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l02-e10","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l02","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Ce qui compte, c’est que tu aies essayé."},"answer":"What matters is that you tried.","accepted_answers":["What matters is you tried.","What matters is that you tried it."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-what-matters-is"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1-e01","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1","position":1,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The plan is cheap. ___, it is easy to start.","translation":"Le plan est bon marché. De plus, il est facile à lancer.","options":["Moreover","However","Although","Unless"]},"answer":"Moreover","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Moreover ajoute une raison dans le même sens ; however marque un contraste.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-moreover"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1","position":2,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Remets les mots dans l’ordre","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["What","worries","me","is","the","cost"],"translation":"Ce qui m’inquiète, c’est le coût."},"answer":"What worries me is the cost.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["efr-what-matters-is"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1","position":3,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"débat"},"answer":"debate","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-debate"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1","position":4,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Le plan est bon marché. De plus, il est facile à lancer."},"answer":"The plan is cheap. Moreover, it is easy to start.","accepted_answers":["The plan is cheap. Moreover, it's easy to start.","The plan is cheap. Furthermore, it is easy to start.","The plan is cheap. Moreover it is easy to start."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-moreover"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1","position":5,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The reason ___ I called is that I need your help.","translation":"La raison pour laquelle j’ai appelé, c’est que j’ai besoin de ton aide.","options":["why","because","what","for"]},"answer":"why","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"The reason why… is that… (pas « is because » dans un registre soutenu).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-the-reason-why"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1","position":6,"type":"complete_word","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Écris le mot en entier","payload":{"type":"complete_word","masked":"f_r_h_r_o_e","hint":"par ailleurs / qui plus est"},"answer":"furthermore","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":20,"words":["efr-furthermore"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1","position":7,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Associe chaque mot à sa signification","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"as a result","right":"par conséquent / c’est pourquoi"},{"left":"debate","right":"débat"},{"left":"moreover","right":"de plus / en outre"},{"left":"the reason why","right":"la raison pour laquelle"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-as-a-result","efr-debate","efr-moreover","efr-the-reason-why"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1","position":8,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Que veut dire « the reason why » ?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"the reason why","options":["la raison pour laquelle","tout bien considéré / tout compte fait","convaincant","par conséquent / c’est pourquoi"]},"answer":"la raison pour laquelle","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["efr-the-reason-why"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1-e09","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1","position":9,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"moreover","options":["moreover","the reason why","nevertheless","point of view"]},"answer":"moreover","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-moreover"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1-e10","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-rev1","position":10,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Que veut dire « as a result » ?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"as a result","options":["par conséquent / c’est pourquoi","tenir compte de / prendre en compte","l’emporter sur / peser plus lourd que","valable / valide"]},"answer":"par conséquent / c’est pourquoi","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["efr-as-a-result"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l03-e01","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l03","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Associe chaque mot à sa signification","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"admittedly","right":"certes / il faut reconnaître que"},{"left":"nevertheless","right":"néanmoins / malgré tout"},{"left":"on the contrary","right":"au contraire"},{"left":"point of view","right":"point de vue"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-admittedly","efr-nevertheless","efr-on-the-contrary","efr-point-of-view"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l03-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"It was difficult. ___, we finished on time.","translation":"C’était difficile. Néanmoins, nous avons fini à temps.","options":["Nevertheless","Moreover","Furthermore","As a result"]},"answer":"Nevertheless","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Nevertheless introduit quelque chose qui se produit malgré ce qui précède.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-nevertheless"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l03-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I'm not tired. On the ___, I feel great.","translation":"Je ne suis pas fatigué. Au contraire, je me sens super bien.","options":["contrary","other","opposite","way"]},"answer":"contrary","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"On the contrary contredit ce qui précède (au contraire). On the other hand ajoute un autre aspect de la même idée (d’un autre côté, par contre) : attention, « par contre » ne se dit pas on the contrary.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-on-the-contrary"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l03-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l03","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-school-debate","setting":"Un débat au lycée : faut-il interdire les téléphones en classe ?","speakers":[{"name":"Moderator","voice":"a"},{"name":"Lucas","voice":"b"},{"name":"Hannah","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Today's debate: should phones be banned in schools? Lucas, you're first."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"Yes, they should. Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school. As a result, many students feel anxious all day."},{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Hannah, your answer?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"But that's an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Fair question. What I'm saying is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"Que concède Hannah et que propose-t-elle à la place ?","options":["Elle reconnaît que les téléphones distraient, mais propose d’apprendre à bien s’en servir","Elle accepte de les interdire","Elle dit qu’ils ne distraient pas","Elle propose de les interdire seulement pendant les examens"]},"answer":"Elle reconnaît que les téléphones distraient, mais propose d’apprendre à bien s’en servir","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Hannah dit : « Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l03-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-free-uni","document":"post","setting":"Une tribune sur l’université gratuite.","title":"Education is an investment, not a cost","lines":["Should university be free? I believe it should.","First, education benefits everyone, not only the student. Educated citizens earn more, pay more taxes and are healthier. Furthermore, free education gives poor students the same chances as rich ones.","Admittedly, free universities cost the government a lot of money, and some people argue that students should pay for their own future. Nevertheless, the long-term benefits outweigh the costs.","It is not the cost of education that should worry us, but the cost of ignorance.","To sum up, free university is not a gift. It is an investment in all of us."]},"question":"Que reconnaît l’autrice et comment le réfute-t-elle ?","options":["Que ça coûte cher à l’État, mais que les bénéfices à long terme sont plus importants","Que c’est injuste, mais nécessaire","Que les étudiants ne l’apprécient pas à sa juste valeur","Que c’est impossible, mais qu’il faut essayer"]},"answer":"Que ça coûte cher à l’État, mais que les bénéfices à long terme sont plus importants","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’article dit : « Admittedly, free universities cost the government a lot of money… Nevertheless, the long-term benefits outweigh the costs ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l03-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l03","position":6,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"I understand your point of view, but I disagree.","options":["I understand your point of view, but I disagree.","I understand your point of view, and I agree.","I don't understand your point of view, but I agree.","I understand your idea, but I disagree."]},"answer":"I understand your point of view, but I disagree.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-point-of-view"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l03-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l03","position":7,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Remets les mots dans l’ordre","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Admittedly","it","is","expensive","but","it","is","worth","it"],"translation":"Certes, c’est cher, mais ça vaut le coup."},"answer":"Admittedly it is expensive but it is worth it.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["efr-admittedly"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l03-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l03","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Réponds en anglais","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"You don't agree with me, do you? (tu comprends son point de vue, mais tu n’es pas d’accord)","translation":"Tu n’es pas d’accord avec moi, hein ?"},"answer":"I understand your point of view, but I disagree.","accepted_answers":["I understand your point of view, but I don't agree.","I understand your point of view but I disagree.","No. I understand your point of view, but I don't agree."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-point-of-view"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l03-e09","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l03","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"C’était difficile. Néanmoins, nous avons fini à temps."},"answer":"It was difficult. Nevertheless, we finished on time.","accepted_answers":["It was hard. Nevertheless, we finished on time.","It was difficult. Nevertheless we finished on time."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-nevertheless"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l04-e01","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Associe chaque mot à sa signification","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"valid","right":"valable / valide"},{"left":"convincing","right":"convaincant"},{"left":"assumption","right":"supposition / hypothèse"},{"left":"take into account","right":"tenir compte de / prendre en compte"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-valid","efr-convincing","efr-assumption","efr-take-into-account"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l04-e02","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"We need to take the costs ___ account.","translation":"Nous devons tenir compte des coûts.","options":["into","in","on","to"]},"answer":"into","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-take-into-account"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l04-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"That's just an ___. Where is the evidence?","translation":"Ce n’est qu’une supposition. Où sont les preuves ?","options":["assumption","argument","opinion","answer"]},"answer":"assumption","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-assumption"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l04-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l04","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-school-debate","setting":"Un débat au lycée : faut-il interdire les téléphones en classe ?","speakers":[{"name":"Moderator","voice":"a"},{"name":"Lucas","voice":"b"},{"name":"Hannah","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Today's debate: should phones be banned in schools? Lucas, you're first."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"Yes, they should. Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school. As a result, many students feel anxious all day."},{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Hannah, your answer?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"But that's an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Fair question. What I'm saying is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"Que reproche Lucas à Hannah ?","options":["Que ce qu’elle dit est une supposition sans preuves","Qu’elle parle trop","Qu’elle a changé d’avis","Qu’elle n’a pas répondu à la question"]},"answer":"Que ce qu’elle dit est une supposition sans preuves","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Lucas dit : « But that’s an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better? ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l04-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-four-days","setting":"Des collègues discutent de la proposition de travailler quatre jours par semaine.","speakers":[{"name":"Olivia","voice":"a"},{"name":"Ken","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"So, the four-day week. What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays?"},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"We'd take turns. The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they're rested."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"That may be true for some jobs. But we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day."},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"That's a valid point. So let's try it for three months and measure the results."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"OK, I find that convincing. All things considered, a trial is a good compromise."}]},"question":"De quoi Olivia demande-t-elle de tenir compte, et que répond Ken ?","options":["Que les clients comptent sur eux tous les jours ; Ken l’admet et propose un essai de trois mois","Que c’est cher ; Ken le nie","Que personne ne veut travailler le vendredi ; Ken se fâche","Que c’est illégal ; Ken en doute"]},"answer":"Que les clients comptent sur eux tous les jours ; Ken l’admet et propose un essai de trois mois","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Olivia : « we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day ». Ken : « That’s a valid point. So let’s try it for three months ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l04-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-tips","document":"post","setting":"Des conseils pour écrire un bon argumentaire.","title":"Writing tips","lines":["How to write a convincing argument","Give reasons, not only opinions. \"I think it is bad\" is a point of view; \"it increases traffic by 30%\" is an argument.","Question your assumptions. If you assume that everyone agrees with you, your argument will be weak.","Take the other side into account. Mention the strongest counterargument and explain why your position is still valid.","Finish clearly. What readers remember is usually the last thing they read."]},"question":"D’après les conseils, quelle différence y a-t-il entre un point de vue et un argument ?","options":["Un argument donne une raison concrète, pas seulement une opinion","Il n’y a pas de différence","L’argument est plus court","Le point de vue utilise des chiffres"]},"answer":"Un argument donne une raison concrète, pas seulement une opinion","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Le texte dit : « \"I think it is bad\" is a point of view; \"it increases traffic by 30%\" is an argument ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l04-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l04","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Her argument was very convincing.","options":["Her argument was very convincing.","Her argument was not very convincing.","His argument was very convincing.","Her answer was very convincing."]},"answer":"Her argument was very convincing.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-convincing"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l04-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l04","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Remets les mots dans l’ordre","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["That","is","a","valid","point"],"translation":"C’est un argument valable."},"answer":"That is a valid point.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["efr-valid"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l04-e09","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l04","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Réponds en anglais","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Did his presentation persuade you? (oui, elle était très convaincante)","translation":"Sa présentation t’a convaincu ?"},"answer":"Yes, it was very convincing.","accepted_answers":["Yes, it was really convincing.","Yes. It was very convincing.","It was very convincing."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["efr-convincing"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l04-e10","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l04","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduis en anglais","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Nous devons tenir compte des coûts."},"answer":"We need to take the costs into account.","accepted_answers"