xplanation_es":"The benefits (pluriel) outweigh.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-outweigh"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l05-e03","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l05","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"To sum ___, I think the plan is a good idea.","translation":"En résumé, je pense que le plan est une bonne idée.","options":["up","out","on","off"]},"answer":"up","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-to-sum-up"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l05-e04","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l05","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-free-uni","document":"post","setting":"Une tribune sur l’université gratuite.","title":"Education is an investment, not a cost","lines":["Should university be free? I believe it should.","First, education benefits everyone, not only the student. Educated citizens earn more, pay more taxes and are healthier. Furthermore, free education gives poor students the same chances as rich ones.","Admittedly, free universities cost the government a lot of money, and some people argue that students should pay for their own future. Nevertheless, the long-term benefits outweigh the costs.","It is not the cost of education that should worry us, but the cost of ignorance.","To sum up, free university is not a gift. It is an investment in all of us."]},"question":"Sur quelle idée l’autrice conclut-elle ?","options":["Que l’université gratuite est un investissement pour tous, pas un cadeau","Que l’université devrait être moins chère","Que les étudiants doivent payer","Que l’État dépense mal"]},"answer":"Que l’université gratuite est un investissement pour tous, pas un cadeau","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’article se termine ainsi : « To sum up, free university is not a gift. It is an investment in all of us ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l05-e05","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l05","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-free-uni","document":"post","setting":"Une tribune sur l’université gratuite.","title":"Education is an investment, not a cost","lines":["Should university be free? I believe it should.","First, education benefits everyone, not only the student. Educated citizens earn more, pay more taxes and are healthier. Furthermore, free education gives poor students the same chances as rich ones.","Admittedly, free universities cost the government a lot of money, and some people argue that students should pay for their own future. Nevertheless, the long-term benefits outweigh the costs.","It is not the cost of education that should worry us, but the cost of ignorance.","To sum up, free university is not a gift. It is an investment in all of us."]},"question":"Que met en relief la phrase « It is not the cost of education that should worry us, but the cost of ignorance » ?","options":["Que ce qui coûte vraiment cher, c’est de ne pas éduquer les gens","Que l’éducation coûte très cher","Que l’ignorance n’a pas de coût","Que l’État devrait dépenser moins"]},"answer":"Que ce qui coûte vraiment cher, c’est de ne pas éduquer les gens","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Avec It is… that…, l’autrice met l’accent sur « the cost of ignorance » (comme « c’est… qui » en français) : ce qui est inquiétant, ce n’est pas de payer l’éducation, mais son absence.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l05-e06","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l05","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-four-days","setting":"Des collègues discutent de la proposition de travailler quatre jours par semaine.","speakers":[{"name":"Olivia","voice":"a"},{"name":"Ken","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"So, the four-day week. What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays?"},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"We'd take turns. The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they're rested."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"That may be true for some jobs. But we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day."},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"That's a valid point. So let's try it for three months and measure the results."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"OK, I find that convincing. All things considered, a trial is a good compromise."}]},"question":"Comment se termine la discussion ?","options":["Olivia est convaincue : un essai de trois mois est un bon compromis","Ils ne se mettent pas d’accord","Ken retire sa proposition","Ils décident de demander au chef"]},"answer":"Olivia est convaincue : un essai de trois mois est un bon compromis","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Olivia dit : « OK, I find that convincing. All things considered, a trial is a good compromise ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l05-e07","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l05","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"All things considered, it was a good year.","options":["All things considered, it was a good year.","All things considered, it was a bad year.","All things considered, it will be a good year.","All in all, it was a good year."]},"answer":"All things considered, it was a good year.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["efr-all-things-considered"]},{"id":"efr-b2-u10-l05-e08","lesson_id":"efr-b2-u10-l05","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Répo