,"normalizer":"polygo.answers.v1","typo_tolerance":true},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.k4et7boap0vbbn","content_hash":"v1:81df9da403298c9f9f944c19c1dfb86f9c8cd23ef92e40ee19475c877e1db22b","prompt_es":"Associe chaque mot à sa signification","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"leader","right":"leader / dirigeant"},{"left":"delegate","right":"déléguer"},{"left":"workload","right":"charge de travail"},{"left":"persuade","right":"convaincre / persuader"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"grading_spec":{"mode":"pair_set","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.weajufkpmyg4ll","content_hash":"v1:2ecbdbe86e0c64648321ef416b784fb96d3c8ad0c24510cbc27f010bf18c419b","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"She took ___ a new project last week.","translation":"Elle a pris en charge un nouveau projet la semaine dernière.","options":["on","up","off","down"]},"answer":"on","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.0z3cxx3eehaak2","content_hash":"v1:1edd7083a6be642187fb920396de15e81b238bf37498eaf62f36cf807d34c3ec","prompt_es":"Complète la phrase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I persuaded my boss ___ me a day off.","translation":"J’ai convaincu mon chef de me donner un jour de congé.","options":["to give","giving","give","gave"]},"answer":"to give","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Persuade someone to + verbe (convaincre quelqu’un de + infinitif).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.r36b6z613jbxwn","content_hash":"v1:cceca51559e173dc0f9c99b4a9b1ffdba4723924565bd6ad2048b2388d851277","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u2-team","setting":"Une cheffe d’équipe parle avec un employé débordé.","speakers":[{"name":"Grace","voice":"a"},{"name":"Omar","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Grace","text":"Omar, you look exhausted. Is your workload too heavy at the moment?"},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Honestly, yes. I took on the new client last month, and I'm still doing my old projects."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"You should have told me. A good leader needs to know these things."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"I didn't want to turn down the client. I thought it was a good opportunity."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"It is, but you can't do everything. Let's delegate the reports to Ben."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Are you sure? He is quite new."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"That's fine. I'll help him at the beginning, in case he has questions."}]},"question":"Pourquoi Omar a-t-il autant de travail ?","options":["Il a pris en charge un nouveau client et continue ses anciens projets","Un collègue a démissionné","Il apprend un nouveau métier","Sa cheffe lui a donné les rapports de Ben"]},"answer":"Il a pris en charge un nouveau client et continue ses anciens projets","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Omar dit : « I took on the new client last month, and I’m still doing my old projects ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.81bgi09jhqpy49","content_hash":"v1:08a2a10f028fac430f20b34fe7ffc39a78780ed8203ab24f84197c6ba854e536","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u2-team","setting":"Une cheffe d’équipe parle avec un employé débordé.","speakers":[{"name":"Grace","voice":"a"},{"name":"Omar","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Grace","text":"Omar, you look exhausted. Is your workload too heavy at the moment?"},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Honestly, yes. I took on the new client last month, and I'm still doing my old projects."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"You should have told me. A good leader needs to know these things."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"I didn't want to turn down the client. I thought it was a good opportunity."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"It is, but you can't do everything. Let's delegate the reports to Ben."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Are you sure? He is quite new."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"That's fine. I'll help him at the beginning, in case he has questions."}]},"question":"Quelle solution Grace propose-t-elle ?","options":["Déléguer les rapports à Ben et l’aider au début","Refuser le nouveau client","Embaucher quelqu’un d’autre","Qu’Omar travaille le week-end"]},"answer":"Déléguer les rapports à Ben et l’aider au début","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Grace dit : « Let’s delegate the reports to Ben… I’ll help him at the beginning ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.d43gsjfrh0j5ct","content_hash":"v1:e84364152013f285d70f11b0229686883dc5b84b2319c0b3621acc81a1037802","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u2-leader","document":"post","setting":"Un article de magazine sur le leadership.","title":"Leaders, not bosses","lines":["What makes a good leader? Many people imagine someone who gives orders and never changes their mind. Research shows the opposite.","The best leaders are flexible. They listen first, and they are willing to compromise when a better idea appears.","They also know how to delegate. Instead of doing everything themselves, they give people responsibility and trust them to do the job.","Finally, they persuade rather than order. When a team understands the reason for a decision, it works harder to make it succeed."]},"question":"D’