 : faut-il interdire les téléphones en classe ?","speakers":[{"name":"Moderator","voice":"a"},{"name":"Lucas","voice":"b"},{"name":"Hannah","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Today's debate: should phones be banned in schools? Lucas, you're first."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"Yes, they should. Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school. As a result, many students feel anxious all day."},{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Hannah, your answer?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"But that's an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Fair question. What I'm saying is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"Quelles raisons Lucas donne-t-il pour interdire les téléphones ?","options":["Ils distraient et facilitent le harcèlement, qui continue après les cours","Ils coûtent cher","Ils se cassent facilement","Les profs ne savent pas s’en servir"]},"answer":"Ils distraient et facilitent le harcèlement, qui continue après les cours","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Lucas dit : « Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.z1lzz3nsby69yh","content_hash":"v1:80c0d6313e40016b6bec86bb216c07d5fd241abcaf76c1814a89e1b9e3799ac2","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-school-debate","setting":"Un débat au lycée : faut-il interdire les téléphones en classe ?","speakers":[{"name":"Moderator","voice":"a"},{"name":"Lucas","voice":"b"},{"name":"Hannah","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Today's debate: should phones be banned in schools? Lucas, you're first."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"Yes, they should. Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school. As a result, many students feel anxious all day."},{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Hannah, your answer?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"But that's an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Fair question. What I'm saying is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"Quelle conséquence Lucas mentionne-t-il ?","options":["Beaucoup d’élèves se sentent anxieux toute la journée","Les élèves ont de mauvaises notes","Les parents se plaignent","L’établissement dépense plus"]},"answer":"Beaucoup d’élèves se sentent anxieux toute la journée","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Lucas dit : « As a result, many students feel anxious all day ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.5bugg7vy2y1u33","content_hash":"v1:402a4165e70c1f595e8eea760827168894da49539e12aa42f78cac2b1da0b64a","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-free-uni","document":"post","setting":"Une tribune sur l’université gratuite.","title":"Education is an investment, not a cost","lines":["Should university be free? I believe it should.","First, education benefits everyone, not only the student. Educated citizens earn more, pay more taxes and are healthier. Furthermore, free education gives poor students the same chances as rich ones.","Admittedly, free universities cost the government a lot of money, and some people argue that students should pay for their own future. Nevertheless, the long-term benefits outweigh the costs.","It is not the cost of education that should worry us, but the cost of ignorance.","To sum up, free university is not a gift. It is an investment in all of us."]},"question":"Quel deuxième argument l’autrice ajoute-t-elle avec furthermore ?","options":["Que l’éducation gratuite donne aux étudiants pauvres les mêmes chances","Que les diplômés paient moins d’impôts","Que les universités sont bon marché","Que les riches ne devraient pas faire d’études"]},"answer":"Que l’éducation gratuite donne aux étudiants pauvres les mêmes chances","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’article dit : « Furthermore, free education gives poor students the same chances as rich ones ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.7kyib189y5up6x","content_hash":"v1:9c6e435cbf98dd0f4f6ac272cb6c89cbec87ad657830c410f4dcad63411eb171","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"We had a debate about social media.","options":["We had a debate about social media.","We had a debate about the news.","We have a debate about social media.","They had a debate about social media."]},"answer":"We had a debate about social media.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.oeqtx11bnfjrox","content_hash":"v1:700b1b9f751dc42d0dda78c0b73e29a11650ddf1d7facf31eaa0706bc447f2a3","prompt_es":"Remets les mots dans l’ordre","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Furthermore","free","education","gives","everyone","the","same","chances"],"translation