e la proposition de travailler quatre jours par semaine.","speakers":[{"name":"Olivia","voice":"a"},{"name":"Ken","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"So, the four-day week. What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays?"},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"We'd take turns. The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they're rested."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"That may be true for some jobs. But we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day."},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"That's a valid point. So let's try it for three months and measure the results."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"OK, I find that convincing. All things considered, a trial is a good compromise."}]},"question":"Qu’est-ce qui inquiète Olivia dans la semaine de quatre jours ?","options":["Qui va s’occuper des clients le vendredi","Gagner moins","Travailler plus d’heures","Que Ken ne soit pas là"]},"answer":"Qui va s’occuper des clients le vendredi","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Olivia dit : « What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays? ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.p2sb0chn8k0nmm","content_hash":"v1:23700b5049fd6436483ec462b4e04c585ebf6ed979d0960f97871acb39bc76dc","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-four-days","setting":"Des collègues discutent de la proposition de travailler quatre jours par semaine.","speakers":[{"name":"Olivia","voice":"a"},{"name":"Ken","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"So, the four-day week. What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays?"},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"We'd take turns. The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they're rested."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"That may be true for some jobs. But we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day."},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"That's a valid point. So let's try it for three months and measure the results."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"OK, I find that convincing. All things considered, a trial is a good compromise."}]},"question":"D’après Ken, pourquoi d’autres entreprises sont-elles passées à la semaine de quatre jours ?","options":["Parce que les gens travaillent mieux quand ils sont reposés","Parce qu’elles économisent de l’argent","Parce que les clients l’ont demandé","Parce que c’est la loi"]},"answer":"Parce que les gens travaillent mieux quand ils sont reposés","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ken dit : « The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they’re rested ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.8ukurvc4ydgecv","content_hash":"v1:b3a8c62c672a89dd17bb85d66476188be83b8c8c9da0d300ad70cba55807b4cc","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-school-debate","setting":"Un débat au lycée : faut-il interdire les téléphones en classe ?","speakers":[{"name":"Moderator","voice":"a"},{"name":"Lucas","voice":"b"},{"name":"Hannah","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Today's debate: should phones be banned in schools? Lucas, you're first."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"Yes, they should. Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school. As a result, many students feel anxious all day."},{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Hannah, your answer?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"But that's an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Fair question. What I'm saying is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"Que précise Hannah avec « In other words… » ?","options":["Qu’avec l’interdiction, les élèves vont juste se servir davantage de leur téléphone à la maison","Que les téléphones sont dangereux","Qu’elle est d’accord avec Lucas","Qu’elle n’a pas de preuves"]},"answer":"Qu’avec l’interdiction, les élèves vont juste se servir davantage de leur téléphone à la maison","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Hannah dit : « a ban doesn’t teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.4na4aemtywgc4p","content_hash":"v1:77d93643b6196fb9d7457c962ebff73cd6fe5e42183629d4dfd2e48f414ff58e","prompt_es":"Écoute et choisis ce que tu entends","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"What matters is that you tried.","options":["What matters is that you tried.","What matters is that you won.","It doesn't matter that you tried.","What matters is that we tried."]},"answer":"What matters is that you tried.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.jmclvknwdfg1b9","content_hash":"v1:53c1904a3c265b3540cfd07a085a8661b718e4d866e678a293a744fd4367df44","prompt_es":"Remets les mots dans l’ordre","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["What","worries","me","is","the","cost"],"translation":"Ce qui m’inquiète, c’est le coût."},"answer":"What worries me is the cost.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"grading_spec":{"mode":"normalized_text","mode_versio