g is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"Que concède Hannah et que propose-t-elle à la place ?","options":["Elle reconnaît que les téléphones distraient, mais propose d’apprendre à bien s’en servir","Elle accepte de les interdire","Elle dit qu’ils ne distraient pas","Elle propose de les interdire seulement pendant les examens"]},"answer":"Elle reconnaît que les téléphones distraient, mais propose d’apprendre à bien s’en servir","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Hannah dit : « Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.mik8n2d2s7vseu","content_hash":"v1:da0e090d88ceb0769e998c020f8a5e680f87e25d314be377cb74893cd9e8309e","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-free-uni","document":"post","setting":"Une tribune sur l’université gratuite.","title":"Education is an investment, not a cost","lines":["Should university be free? I believe it should.","First, education benefits everyone, not only the student. Educated citizens earn more, pay more taxes and are healthier. Furthermore, free education gives poor students the same chances as rich ones.","Admittedly, free universities cost the government a lot of money, and some people argue that students should pay for their own future. Nevertheless, the long-term benefits outweigh the costs.","It is not the cost of education that should worry us, but the cost of ignorance.","To sum up, free university is not a gift. It is an investment in all of us."]},"question":"Que reconnaît l’autrice et comment le réfute-t-elle ?","options":["Que ça coûte cher à l’État, mais que les bénéfices à long terme son