theless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"But that's an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Fair question. What I'm saying is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"Que reproche Lucas à Hannah ?","options":["Que ce qu’elle dit est une supposition sans preuves","Qu’elle parle trop","Qu’elle a changé d’avis","Qu’elle n’a pas répondu à la question"]},"answer":"Que ce qu’elle dit est une supposition sans preuves","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Lucas dit : « But that’s an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better? ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.816uzygvnjkv27","content_hash":"v1:26d34b799a8df16304123f13ceaa43d588436d2c15973fbf53a958bdfd72536b","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-four-days","setting":"Des collègues discutent de la proposition de travailler quatre jours par semaine.","speakers":[{"name":"Olivia","voice":"a"},{"name":"Ken","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"So, the four-day week. What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays?"},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"We'd take turns. The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they're rested."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"That may be true for some jobs. But we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day."},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"That's a valid point. So let's try it for three months and measure the results."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"OK, I find that convincing. All things considered, a trial is a good compromise."}]},"question":"De quoi Olivia demande-t-elle de tenir compte, et que répond Ken ?","options":["Que les clients comptent sur eux tous les jours ; Ken l’admet et propose un essai de trois mois","Que c’est cher ; Ken le nie","Que personne ne veut travailler le vendredi ; Ken se fâche","Que c’est illégal ; Ken en doute"]},"answer":"Que les clients comptent sur eux tous les jours ; Ken l’admet et propose un essai de trois mois","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Olivia : « we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day ». Ken : « That’s a valid point. So let’s try it for three months ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.yfba32rh64itgv","content_hash":"v1:aa67546010a6fdcac3002ef62a7fbd9c7832a5495e10a13971e54aae909020ea","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u10-tips","document":"post","setting":"Des conseils pour écrire un bon argumentaire.","title":"Writing tips","lines":["How to write a convincing argument","Give reasons, not only opinions. \"I think it is bad\" is a point of view; \"it increases traffic by 30%\" is an argument.","Question your assumptions. If you assume that everyone agrees with you, your argument will be weak.","Take the other side into account. Mention the strongest counterargument and explain why your position is still valid.","Finish clearly. What readers remember is usually the last thing they read."]},"question":"D’après les conseils, quelle différence y a-t-il entre un point de vue et un argument ?","options":["Un argument donne une raison concrète, pas seulement une opinion","Il n’y a pas de différence","L’argument est plus court","Le point de vue utilise des chiffres"]},"answer":"Un argument donne une raison concrète, pas seulement une opinion","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Le texte dit : « \"I think it is bad\" is a point of view; \"it increases traf