ers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.y3qlgxkhakts2t","content_hash":"v1:d412fff8d8d5a57578a35b1c9579e2271e51c0b3ae6bea8b00918e420d95330a","prompt_es":"Écoute et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"efr.stim.b2-u12-job-offer","setting":"Une amie raconte à une autre qu’elle doit décider si elle déménage pour le travail.","speakers":[{"name":"Alice","voice":"a"},{"name":"Rosa","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Alice","text":"I've got a real dilemma. The Lisbon office has offered me a job as team manager."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"That's amazing! So why do you look worried?"},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"Because I'd have to move in a month. I've been weighing up the pros and cons all week."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"What does your gut feeling say?"},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"To go. But I'm having second thoughts because of my parents. They're getting older."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"Remember two years ago, when you turned down the job in Berlin? If you had taken it, you'd be speaking German by now."},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"I know. And if I were braver, I would have said yes immediately this time too."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"Every choice has a trade-off. But Lisbon is only a short flight away. You could visit them often."}]},"question":"Quel est le dilemme d’Alice ?","options":["Accepter ou non un poste à Lisbonne et déménager dans un mois","Changer ou non de carrière","Déménager ou non à Berlin","Quitter ou non son travail pour s’occuper de ses parents"]},"answer":"Accepter ou non un poste à Lisbonne et déménager dans un mois","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Alice dit : « I’ve got a real dilemma. The Lisbon office has offered me a job as team manager… I’d have to move in a month ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.pi1tp2jg9qxict","content_hash":"v1:4687be9ac2c4a4e647fa669b994c3a708ed81fbb03745ad573986e5c0a00fb4c","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u12-guide","document":"post","setting":"Un article sur la façon de prendre des décisions importantes.","title":"How to make a big decision","lines":["Big decisions are hard because there is always a trade-off: more money but less free time, adventure but less security.","First, write down the pros and cons. Seeing them on paper helps you weigh them up more calmly.","Second, ask yourself what is really at stake. Will this matter in five years? If not, do not spend weeks on it.","Third, listen to your gut feeling. Research suggests that our first reaction often contains information we are not aware of.","Finally, accept that no decision is perfect. If we had a crystal ball, we would never make mistakes. We do not, so we learn from them."]},"question":"D’après l’article, pourquoi les grandes décisions sont-elles difficiles ?","options":["Parce qu’on gagne toujours quelque chose en échange d’autre chose qu’on perd","Parce qu’on n’a jamais d’informations","Parce que les gens manquent d’assurance","Parce qu’elles prennent beaucoup de temps"]},"answer":"Parce qu’on gagne toujours quelque chose en échange d’autre chose qu’on perd","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’article dit : « there is always a trade-off: more money but less free time, adventure but less security ».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"efr.ex.ew9cn6hxer9h4v","content_hash":"v1:3ef1f690098216430d497219ce24465eb3d7339708c69edabeaa56a722b44233","prompt_es":"Lis et réponds","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"efr.stim.b2-u12-guide","document":"post","settin